{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod","id":1484258,"title":"How come Vampires always used as a punching bag within the WOD?!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-16T21:07:08-07:00","id":1484258,"title":"How come Vampires always used as a punching bag within the WOD?!","content":"It feels like vampires have become something of a running joke within the WOD game lines, whenever I read a post that talks about vampires going against the other splats, almost everyone in the comment section simultaneously goes &quot;The vampire dies because 'Insert splat' is too strong&quot;. I have even read books which open with the main splat absolutely demolishing the vampire in question, no matter who it is. Yet I have never seen something like that happen in a vampire book. And when people do bring up the one thing vampires are supposed to have a lot of, which is their immense political and criminal influence within cities, I immediately begin to doubt that. Mostly due to how multiple books have already gone over how many of the other splats also have immense criminal and political influence within cities as well, and maybe other areas such as the umbra.<br /> <br /> The werewolves have the Silver fangs and the Shadow lords who seem to have kinfolk in different positions in multiple organizations, both legal and illegal. The bone gnawers seem to have immense influence among the poor, plus the glass walkers seem to have mastery of technology, and lets not forget about the other tribes and fera. Mages have the technocracy, and no doubt the traditions and crafts also have influence within both legal and illegal organizations. Demons have their cults, some of which have immense influence within the city they are located in. Witch hunters and the imbued seem to have some sort of organization behind them such as the Society of Leopold. I could write more but you all probably see where I'm going with this.<br /> <br /> A lot of times a vampires influence doesn't seem to even help. Who cares if that venture elder controls a City Hall? Nothings stopping a werewolf from jumping out of the umbra and setting them on fire, nothings stopping a mage from using coincidental magic to do the same thing, nothing stopping the society of Leopold from doing a drive by in public. Seeing as how vampires are hated by practically everything in the world of darkness, I am legitimately surprised that the denizens of the umbra, such as spirits and wraiths, haven't jumped out and started demolishing every haven.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even make sense why they are the most hated.<br /> <br /> The two other main splats are just as bad as vampires. The Technocracy and other magic factions really want control/freedom to do whatever they want at the end of the day and so do the werewolves and their tribes. This isn't so dissimilar to what vampires want. But for some reason a vampire is always going to be seen as the bigger evil, just because their &quot;damned&quot;. Whats that suppose to even mean? They're damned because they drink blood? Hell, the amount of blood a vampire needs night to night doesn't seem like that big of an issue, as long as they have a bit of restraint they can leave their prey alive and go on their merry way. They're undead, so that makes them perversions against the natural order? Well mages can, and have become immortal in more ways than one, and have been known to manipulate reality to their whims. Werewolves are creatures that have a human body but an animals souls (simplification, but you get what I am trying to say), and have at one point in time tried to limit/exterminate humanity and have exterminated multiple fera who had important duties. They can turn others into vampires? Most don't want the competition. The ones who recklessly do are usually destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-17-2022, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T21:11:07-07:00","id":1484259,"title":"","content":"Can you list specific examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T21:32:02-07:00","id":1484260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484259#post1484259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you list specific examples?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the blood treachery where the hermetics attack a tremere chantry the strike force clears the tremere pretty easily.<br /> <br /> In a couple tribe books whenever they go against a vamp they take minimum casualties compare to the vamps, the silver fangs do take a couple fatalities in the shadow lord tribe book, but it's latter on revealed to have been put into motion by a shadowlord, so in other words the vamps were the suckers. In another tribe book I cant remember a pack of werewolves alboslutely demolish their vampire opponents with no casualties and only a couple heavy injuries. The pack battled the vamps on a basketball course, and they originally didnt know the person they were meetin vas a vamp because they hid their scent. Same happened in the previous encounter I mentioned which occured with a setite who was acting like dumb fledgeling even though he knew a good amount of sorcery which shows he was a neonate, even with the element of surprise and a plan that should have guaranteed victory they were still beat by werewolves attacking head on. there was some more but I cant remember properly.<br /> <br /> Even in their own clanbooks vampires are terrified of mages and werewolves. In the section of both splats that talk about vampires it seems both have immense hatred of kindered but not as much to each other .<br /> <br /> Sorry, kind of sloppy, on phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T21:52:36-07:00","id":1484261,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a nice numerical advantage when it comes to the position for &quot;punching bags&quot;<br /> Most of them are Humans who &quot;just&quot; tuned undead, recived a blood-transmitted curse and just got a set of problems<br /> The 90% of the Vampires of the World are either Fledgelings, neonate or ancillae at best, usually less than 50 years under their belt, and contrary to popular belief, ro be a vampire is not cool. It sucks. You have power? Yes. Powers that came from your damned nature or cursed blood or both. With tha added bonus, you are doomed to fail, thanks to Uriel's curse: &quot;Caine and his childer to cling to Darkness, drink only blood, eat only ashes, and be frozen at the point of death, cursed so all they touch would crumble into nothing.&quot; if you are really serious. Blood-addiction, the Beast, the superiors (not necessarily elders, just others who are a tiny bit better than you) whole set of problems... and at the end of the day, they were just human.<br /> When it comes to the Big Boys? They pull serious punches and deffinitly not punching bags. It is just we see more of the young ones, who are yet to become powerfull<br /> Think it like the Worf Effect<br /> Want a quick way to show how dangerous one of your unknown characters is? Simple, make them do well or win in a fight with a character that the audience already knows is tough. This establishes them as willing to fight and marks them as sufficiently dangerous. For new villains, it's common for them to pick up the toughest character among the heroes and hurl them across the room or otherwise take them out in one blow, thus showing that they are the real deal. It's even a genuinely good strategy \u2014 take out the biggest and toughest in a group, and the rest will accept how tough you are instead of having to prove it over and over. When used sparingly and appropriately, this is a powerful way to establish said villain as a serious and credible threat, leaving the audience thinking, &quot;Wow, they just beat up Worf! They must be bad news!&quot; Named for the tendency in Star Trek: The Next Generation for hostile creatures to do that very thing to Worf.<br /> Vampires can be and eventually became powerhouses, but since they are basically the most numerous supernaturals (except the Hsien, but they are fragile) and have a very strange learning and power curve, they are simply fall in to this category; they are the Worfs of WoD, even when they are weak, just because they will be strong<br /> But in reality even the youngest and weakest vampires could be a really bad news, simply becasue they were Human - they share this with the Kuei Jin, except those crawled back from Hell and learned something - and this makes them one of the most dangerous things in WoD. Humans with powers and desperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T22:17:30-07:00","id":1484263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod#post1484258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't even make sense why they are the most hated.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the other splats are still bitter than a Malkavian went Deadpool, broke the forth wall, and revealed that they get all the plot armor because vampires sell the most books.<br /> <br /> A bit more seriously, vampires were written first, and everyone else is somewhat of a reaction to them, and VtM 1e implying every splat hates every other splats, while as the WoD grew, most of the splats have at least some significant avenues of at least coexistence with each other. Oddly the Technocracy and the Camarilla are generally on pretty good terms mind you.<br /> <br /> There's also plenty of fan annoyance at how various things play out. Vampires in the fiction of the game world regularly come out alive if not victorious against creatures that might not be all powerful, but are certainly fighting on their terms. For example the Tremere survived the First Massasa War with the Order of Hermes (during the Dark Ages, when the Hermetics were far stronger than in modern nights), while also fighting the Omen War against the Tzimisce/Gangrel/Nosferatu. This is ~200 years after the first members of the Tremere became vampires, so in an incredibly short amount of time, they converted the House into a Clan, mastered Thaumaturgy and Gargoyle creation, kept this massive conspiracy under wraps long enough, and were suddenly powerful to be fighting two major supernatural wars. The First Massasa War also was supposedly ended because the Order of Reason kicking off the Ascension War proper... but baring the fall of Mistridge (caused in part by a Tremere) that didn't actually come into play for almost a century where the Order just... stopped caring about the Tremere's betrayal.<br /> <br /> And then you have the Second Massasa War detailed in Blood Treachery that basically gutted the Order of Hermes, while Clan Tremere suffered no meaningful loses that they couldn't Embrace their way back to full strength in a few years.... despite incidents like the one you noted.<br /> <br /> There was a recent thread complaining about how vampires see werewolves as ultra-dangerous death machines, and the Garou mechanics don't exactly refute that, but in the VtM books it's an annoyingly common thing to see, &quot;this vampire has killed a bunch of lupines,&quot; to demonstrate how powerful this NPC is, while the Garou almost never get shown being able to kill any vampires of note without it being a massive and catastrophic Pyrrhic victory for them.<br /> <br /> Until C20 came out, vampires generally had extremely high Banality ratings and many could kill a changeling without even realizing it by being in the same room as them. Wraiths consistently get the short end of the stick all over because everyone gets really potent necromancy powers in their rule sets, but Vampire has the most overtly hostile groups towards treating ghosts as beings to help instead of used as pawns.<br /> <br /> So... vampires keep getting teed up as major threats, even when it doesn't seem justified, and then they win or at least come out with a draw they quickly bounce back from, whenever this comes to a head in a crossover supplement. So the fans generally don't entirely like that and it bleeds into how discussions go about various topics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T22:27:02-07:00","id":1484264,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a lot of advantages. They half bludgeoning damage, can buff physical stats with blood, and can grow they're numbers faster then a rabbit on Easter. That said, they're the &quot;punching bags&quot; because young vampires are nothing compared to literally everything else. Except wraith, they suck.<br /> <br /> In terms of power, vampires only get stronger with age. However, to werewolves who fight corrupting spirits and monsters who are naturally more powerful then the leeches, they tend to be more skin to a minor annoyance. It's like find cockroaches and ants in the kitchen, you're gunning for the roaches before the ants.<br /> <br /> Vampires can be dangerous in WoD, but mostly when the element of time is involved, or they're not afraid to waste blood. Even a new born vampire can buff up to 10 Dexterity out of fear, and wipe the floor with almost anyone. Granted this requires a ton of blood, and only lasts 3 turns before dropping to 6 for the scene, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Also, they can reproduce way too easily. If they wanted to, the world could all be vampires in about a week. Even wraiths can't guarantee a new wraith's creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T22:30:32-07:00","id":1484265,"title":"","content":"Early on they decided that vampires would be the &quot;social&quot; splat, which really doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Vampires are solitary predators who only reluctantly work with each other, generally hunt alone meaning they have no one but themselves to save them if attacked while hunting, and sleep during the day when social abilities are the most useful. They have the strongest in-story need to be formidable in single combat, since they are the most likely to need to settle matters solo, and to do so quickly before the sun rises and renders them helpless.<br /> <br /> Literally every other splat has a stronger claim to being social. Werewolves are pack-creatures who have access to an entire separate universe of allies, and who can use their social abilities in broad daylight. There is a much stronger justification for making werewolves weak in straight-combat because their social abilities more than compensate.<br /> <br /> But no, vampires are the &quot;social&quot; splat, and so must be a joke in straight combat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T01:32:41-07:00","id":1484270,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's really what the early designers meant with the Big 3 and the arena breakdown. Vampires aren't the &quot;social splat&quot; in the sense of &quot;they're the most powerful social characters,&quot; but in the sense of their primary narrative conflicts resolving around the social arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T02:08:14-07:00","id":1484275,"title":"","content":"-revised screwed up the soaking rules for vampires. They would be much more martially competitive were you to use older rules (and I do)<br /> -most vamps are solitary and aren't expecting or looking for third party trouble. <br /> -Attackers have big advantage over defenders on both a tactical and strategic level. Attackers choose when and where to attack, defenders do not. Choosing your battles lets you pick easy victories and avoid even fights or hard. <br /> <br /> If vampires seriously decided they need to work together to eliminate all the lupines and mages and they were incensed enough to bear a few losses, they could do so within a month. They outnumber both factions put together and can easily access overpowering assets like Dominate and the Blood bond. Wartime vampires are scary things. The issue is, Vampires are rarely in wartime; the Jyhad is a slow burn and nominal peace is the best option for most. Werewolves are always in wartime. Mages and Werewolves already have a lot of enemies. Vampires only really seriously consider eachother and humanity as a whole as an everyday threat. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T16:16:28-07:00","id":1484307,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that the main strengths of Vampires, specifically Cainite ones is that those strengths are not table top friendly. The ability for vampires to Dominate/Presence/Blood Bond anyone, at any time has heavy invasion of the body snatchers kind of potential. Add on to this the fact that the fluff routinely refers to vampiric levels of wealth/money individually exceeding whole countries and corporations means whom ever they can't directly access with their powers, they can just buy the services or allegiance of.<br /> <br /> Then the fact that they can replace their numbers in a matter of hours, rather than waiting for years/decades for a new shifter or mage to be born means vampires have the horde faction potential, if not for the masquerade thing.<br /> <br /> All in all, this makes for great antagonist material. Endless resources and minions that the heroes have to wade through. But it kind of falls apart when it is the heroes who deal with everything by remote control. It isn't engaging for many players or even writers for that matter.<br /> <br /> If modern vampires acted how they should, rather than how the fluff forces them to act, then each vampire would live in a converted missile silo, with a private live in herd, and only interacts with most of vampire society by online meetings. If a problem arises, then they hire a mercenary company to deal with it or if fire power isn't enough they hire/own a law firm.<br /> <br /> For some reason &quot;Vampire Lawyers&quot; feels like a redundant statement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Regardless vampires are the most vulnerable of the splats due to being not only damaged by sunlight, but forced into an unconscious state during daytime. Combine this with the potential for using money and minions to solve their problems, then of course they will get written up as the faction to pulp in all interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T17:23:32-07:00","id":1484316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484270#post1484270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's really what the early designers meant with the Big 3 and the arena breakdown. Vampires aren't the &quot;social splat&quot; in the sense of &quot;they're the most powerful social characters,&quot; but in the sense of their primary narrative conflicts resolving around the social arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The Kindred, especially the Camarilla, essentially live in a world akin to Mean Girls, Heathers, Jawbreaker, and Cruel Intentions. And that is on the good nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T18:35:24-07:00","id":1484318,"title":"","content":"What? Vampires the laughing stock? Lol.<br /> <br /> I personally hate the bloodsuckers because I am a Mage obviously... And no, it's not because of the &quot;curse&quot;, or the &quot;blood drinking&quot; stuff, or the &quot;unnatural undead&quot;... Sure, Im not a fan of their disgusting physiology, but I would also want to rid Earth from all the werebeasts too for much the same reason.<br /> <br /> But the reason why I (as a Mage) hate vampires above ALL else, is because vampires are DANGEROUS. I fear them. I dont fear Werewolves or other beasts.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the most powerful faction/organization/conspiracy of the WoD is the Technocracy, hands down. Those are the top dogs.<br /> <br /> But the most powerful INDIVIDUALS are, undoubtly, vampires. The only reason they dont mop the floor with everybody else is that each vampire is the worse enemy of all others. They are the most disunited of all, and if a pack of werewolves were to kill a small group of 6 vampires, there would be 20 others thanking the favor.<br /> <br /> Vampires are the ONLY &quot;race&quot; of the WoD that I genuinely FEAR. Which is why finding a lone one, unprepared and undefended, is too good a chance to let it pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T19:12:47-07:00","id":1484323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484307#post1484307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that the main strengths of Vampires, specifically Cainite ones is that those strengths are not table top friendly. .</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice, every gameline is about fancy parties, detective work, and asskicking. If you are playing vampire, the fancy parties are blood feasts or Elysium. If you are playing werewolf, the fancy party is usually either at a cairn, or a Silver Fang mansion. If you are playing Mage, the party can be at some truly insane locations. But they are a big part of every game. Detective work is pretty much the same in every game. There's a mystery, the players run around looking for clues. Asskicking is pretty much the same in every game, except vampires need the biggest amount of plot armor to survive it, since they spend so much time either hunting alone, or sleeping in utter helplessness. Somehow that werewolf never seems to attack when the coterie are separated hunting for food, or attacks during the day, or brings his own pack. No, he always solo jumps the coterie while they are all together. Very nice of him to act like a video game boss.<br /> <br /> The main supposed advantage of vampires, being able to blood-bond and create ghouls and progeny, isn't really useful most of the time in situations younger vampires find themselves in. It's not relevant at fancy parties. It's not relevant during detective work. It's only occasionally relevant in combat, because you have one human with a parlor-trick watching your back. Compared to werewolves and mages, it's all nothing. Yet it's used as justification for making vampires the weakest race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T02:52:24-07:00","id":1484341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484323#post1484323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In practice, every gameline is about fancy parties, detective work, and asskicking. If you are playing vampire, the fancy parties are blood feasts or Elysium. If you are playing werewolf, the fancy party is usually either at a cairn, or a Silver Fang mansion. If you are playing Mage, the party can be at some truly insane locations. But they are a big part of every game. Detective work is pretty much the same in every game. There's a mystery, the players run around looking for clues. Asskicking is pretty much the same in every game, except vampires need the biggest amount of plot armor to survive it, since they spend so much time either hunting alone, or sleeping in utter helplessness. Somehow that werewolf never seems to attack when the coterie are separated hunting for food, or attacks during the day, or brings his own pack. No, he always solo jumps the coterie while they are all together. Very nice of him to act like a video game boss.<br /> <br /> The main supposed advantage of vampires, being able to blood-bond and create ghouls and progeny, isn't really useful most of the time in situations younger vampires find themselves in. It's not relevant at fancy parties. It's not relevant during detective work. It's only occasionally relevant in combat, because you have one human with a parlor-trick watching your back. Compared to werewolves and mages, it's all nothing. Yet it's used as justification for making vampires the weakest race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, despite playing V:tM and the other WoD lines since the mid 90s, there were very few parties in the games I played in or STed for. Probably this had more to do with the tastes of the people I played with, but the social gathering aspect was rare. There was plenty of detective work, usually in the early game, and asskicking was required when you couldn't avoid combat.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest difference was that many groups play a group of characters that show up in the storyline to move through it or figure it out. It's a passive way to play the game. You show up, you are presented with NPCs and situations to interact with and resolve problems.<br /> <br /> The groups I usually played with were more goal oriented, which is to say they didn't care who had said what at the last meeting in Elysium and cared more about advancing their own plans. Survival and security were paramount, where as random social interaction was seen as an impediment.<br /> <br /> As for combat, we usually played with smart NPC opponents, i.e. the werewolf would attack during the day or when the coterie was hungry and hunting, usually with a bunch of pack mates or kinfolk. Needless to say, this survival of the fittest style of game play meant that most standard story hooks don't work because no one in their right mind would take the security risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T11:27:01-07:00","id":1484374,"title":"","content":"Ghouls with military backgrounds and a decent amount of silver &gt; Garou <br /> One on one, the Garou is a likely victor. Hell there's a few old monsters that can cut through a thousand ghouls in a row before they fall<br /> <br /> However, a single vampire can replace as many ghouls as they want within 3 days. Garou replacements are measured in years. And those old monsters? Doomed to die of old age while their potential replacements are killed off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T11:56:14-07:00","id":1484375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484374#post1484374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls with military backgrounds and a decent amount of silver &gt; Garou<br /> One on one, the Garou is a likely victor. Hell there's a few old monsters that can cut through a thousand ghouls in a row before they fall<br /> <br /> However, a single vampire can replace as many ghouls as they want within 3 days. Garou replacements are measured in years. And those old monsters? Doomed to die of old age while their potential replacements are killed off.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't replace your ghouls if you're killed while solo punching hobos for food in an alleyway, or a while solo seducing someone in a nightclub to go off somewhere private with you, or while solo breaking into someone's house to feed on them while they sleep. It's just not practical to go around surrounded by ghouls because vampires are solo predators who depend heavily on stealth, even the ones who hunt via seduction depend on stealth in the sense of being unobtrusive.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are extremely well-equiped to cut through stealth like it was air, and their pack nature means they are much better designed to actually group up to kill a target. Effectively, it's a wolfpack versus a solo animal like a cat.<br /> <br /> And, of course, they have their own backup: spirits, some of which can manifest in the material world and kick ass all on their own.<br /> <br /> Even without spirit backup, and even with the ghouls armed with silver, I'm betting on the werewolves. They have ways of countering silver, and they are insanely fast and strong.<br /> <br /> In fact, it's telling that if you have a werewolf NPC in a vampire game, the werewolf pretty much has to fight stupid for the players to win. Whereas if you have vampire NPCs in a werewolf game, the vampire NPCs not only have to fight smart, they have to be unnaturally on guard for solo predators. They have to be constantly surrounded by a degree of security that a solo stealth predator just wouldn't be most of the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T13:35:14-07:00","id":1484382,"title":"","content":"As the relative variety of answers show, this is a complex question.<br /> <br /> My first point so is to bring up that the <i>setting</i> isn't a Battle Royal, it is an ecosystem. The splats occupy their own niches and have limited ways of perceiving and interacting with one another. When it happens, it is always in a context. So here's one of the things <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> said about the advantage of attackers: whenever you see a scene of conflict, by definition it isn't those splats in their usual circumstances, but already the culmination of a series of events. You can reasonably expect that whomever is attacking is going to win just because they managed to do the attack to begin with, unless they're idiots.<br /> <br /> Further examining the Big 3 (because things are far more nuanced outside them), this impression heavily comes from their themes and the situations where they interact. Werewolves are, as a splat, warriors. So even if not everyone of them is indeed a warrior, they have more combat-oriented innate abilities, <i>more combat-oriented individuals and <u>usually interact for combat</u></i>. So any werewolf that you find is likely to have a more combat-oriented build simply because they're more common and otherwise they wouldn't be there.<br /> <br /> Werewolves also live in other places and have other enemies, they seldom have any reason to interact with Vampires at all. Even the Glass Walkers aren't likely to just wander the streets at night looking for vampires, they have lots of better things to do with their time, and so do the Bone Gnawers. And if any encounter happens, it is likely that both splats will just avoid each other afterwards to not risk confrontation under non-optimal circumstances. They want to live more than to kill. Finally, they're simply not numerous. The number of Garou in any single country will hardly be greater than 1 to 300 thousand humans and probably less than this, and they don't simply replenish easily. So all together, it is too hard to have chance encounters between the splats, more probable for any confrontation to be the Garou attacking someone who failed at hiding their tracks.<br /> <br /> The Mages are even fewer, and their stronger trope is that a prepared Mage can do virtually anything, including beating up anyone. This is not just with Vampires, but the downside to it is the &quot;prepared&quot; bit. In this regard, you don't get to see Vampires beating the hell out of a Mage so frequently just because putting a werewolf there to do that is funnier, vampires are usually making a fool of the unprepared Mage. They could easily switch, though, Mages can really be caught off-guard and be screwed royally by anyone. But the caveat to the advantage of the attacker is that a Chantry will usually be heavily protected, playing in their preparedness, so getting the better of a Mage in their own turf isn't so easy. Finally their preparedness and curiosity also means that you'll also have particular Mages messing with all sorts of things, like experimenting with Vampires and Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a paranoid bunch. Any inter-splat interaction already means things probably aren't going as the vampire planned, since the typical vampire will plan to get information without ever giving up any, much less exposing themselves to risk. Your successful Kindred may be capable of ripping a werewolf without effort, but is also unlikely to try. They're nocturnal, secretive and city-bound, so they have less opportunities for chance encounters and less engagement with the strange. Their numbers are compensated by this tendency to stay out of sight from everything and everyone at all costs. And most of their activities are equally subtle, keeping a low profile even for the standards of the supernatural. So when a vampire goes physical with other splats, it is likely that they already failed anyway, probably are the weak ones, possibly set-up by their enemies and going against tough attackers.<br /> <br /> Being hated is another tricky bit. Mostly it was a strong 1st edition theme of everyone being at each others throats, that was slowly dropped as a general rule and kept to specific circumstances. As a society, werewolves are purist zealots that have a sworn enmity to anything Wyrm-Tainted, and simple lack of contact and knowledge does the rest, so many of them hate vampires on a matter of principle. Most won't ever find one, though, and in practice individuals are individuals, unease truces and even friendships between them, albeit rare, are a trope on itself. Outside the Euthanatoi Mages mostly don't have many fixed opinions on vampires. Other splats don't give a damn, Changelings and Mummies party with vampires with some frequency, Demons are curious about them, Hunters Hunt, but some even Hunt under the patronage of a vampire.<br /> <br /> On the matter of political influence, it is important to understand that it may be a lot of different things and accomplished in a lot of ways. The reason why Vampires do have the upper hand is, simply put, because this is their main game. Others also know how to play influence, but it is a secondary matter for them, while for vampires it is the core of the job. Here methods, numbers and reaching are a big difference. Typically a Mage has very broad influence, but little dept. They can pull strings all over the world, but their goals are to influence thought and ideology more than to micromanage things, and they pull things by control of a few key pieces. Kinfolk are good, but they're not nearly as numerous as humans themselves, so they're a big help, but still limited in many ways, and their attention is focused to few interests. Vampires do collectively micromanage the entire system in comparison, a tighter, more robust and widespread web of manipulations kept by a horde of dedicated and stealth spiders.<br /> <br /> Each method has its ups and downs, but usually in the context of a possible direct confrontation the Kindred method will be the best, simply because it means more warning for immediate threats and more &quot;direct&quot; means to deal with it. Which is what their web is meant to do, instead of influencing the thoughts of the masses about technology or funding eco-terrorism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T14:57:17-07:00","id":1484387,"title":"","content":"What does &quot;political influence&quot; mean in practice, anyway? It's not like they can use it to get an army surrounding them. It does mean they can decide to have City Park turned into a parking lot, but if a bunch of werewolves decide to kill them for doing this, that political influence means jack. What, concretely, not some vague stuff about influence, what concretely can a vampire do to survive when it's a solo predator who spends a lot of time out punching hobos, seducing in nightclubs, and sneaking into homes to snack on sleepers? What are they gonna do? Have a gang of ghouls surround them as they do that? Really picture that: a vampire who depends on Obfuscate to B&amp;E into homes constantly having a group of ghouls packing silver shotguns crawling through the window with him, or all lounging right outside the house. Or a the vampire who seduces in nightclubs always having a pack of armed ghouls around her as she tries to seduce tonight's guy to go off alone with her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T15:26:50-07:00","id":1484390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484387#post1484387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, concretely, not some vague stuff about influence, what concretely can a vampire do to survive when it's a solo predator who spends a lot of time out punching hobos, seducing in nightclubs, and sneaking into homes to snack on sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not get into a fight, to begin with.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't instantly aware of every Vampire in the street as they step in. Even Gifts like Sense Wyrm and Scent of True Form need active usage with limited reach and rolls that can fail. There's no such a thing as the Garou finding out a vampire just by bumping into them in the night. Obfuscate is an excellent example of a power that will almost guarantee you'll never have to fight one if you don't do anything hugely stupid. And this isn't being powerless, this is the power working as intended.<br /> <br /> Plan an attack after finding about your enemy instead of waiting for being attacked. With a full Blood Pool, prepared and armed for it, it isn't any impossible task to use Disciplines and stuff to deal with Garou, despite how much some people believe otherwise. You ignore here that your proposed scenario has the Vampire at disadvantage to begin with. Also, predators in nature are always wary of things that can go wrong while they're hunting, unless they're desperate.<br /> <br /> A vampire will hardly win a direct fight against a werewolf, but insisting that they should is to ignore the difference in context and theme, while insisting in what is actually an extremely specific scenario. And no, they shouldn't be the toughest, meanest fighters around when they're human predators versus werewolves being warriors fighting Cthulhu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T16:17:42-07:00","id":1484394,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I just think that vamps suffered from the fact of being the first game of the line, they already had a set system with enough complexities regarding lore and disciplines that modifying it to bring vamps in line with other splats is just not feasible besides not really being necessary in the first place since vampire consistently outsold and outperform all the other lines of WoD.<br /> <br /> Regarding their combat prowess or lack of thereoff compared to the other splats, that really didn't bother me much since I enjoy the sense of vulnerability that comes with not really being the apex predator, what really bothered me is that the other splats outperform vamps even in the fields where they should supposedly have an edge, mainly in the social aspect of the game where werewolves and changelings (I won't even put mages in here since they can do literally anything anyway) have abilities that put vamps disciplines to shame. I have played in multisplat games (you really shouldn't since the system is not designed for that but still) and it became pretty clear to me that vamps are quite simply redundant compared to the other splats, I'm not talking about a particular discipline or anything, just from a purely niche perspective, there is nothing that vamps can do that other splats can't do better which is one of the reasons why I switched to CoD since I felt that it handled vampires (and all the other splats too to be honest) much better than WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T17:07:36-07:00","id":1484400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484387#post1484387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &amp;quot;political influence&amp;quot; mean in practice, anyway? It's not like they can use it to get an army surrounding them. It does mean they can decide to have City Park turned into a parking lot, but if a bunch of werewolves decide to kill them for doing this, that political influence means jack. What, concretely, not some vague stuff about influence, what concretely can a vampire do to survive when it's a solo predator who spends a lot of time out punching hobos, seducing in nightclubs, and sneaking into homes to snack on sleepers? What are they gonna do? Have a gang of ghouls surround them as they do that? Really picture that: a vampire who depends on Obfuscate to B&amp;E into homes constantly having a group of ghouls packing silver shotguns crawling through the window with him, or all lounging right outside the house. Or a the vampire who seduces in nightclubs always having a pack of armed ghouls around her as she tries to seduce tonight's guy to go off alone with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are not dumb, quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> What the &quot;lone vampire&quot; will do will be to inform his elder about &quot;lupine activity&quot; in the city. The elder will say &quot;thank you&quot;, the neonate will receive some token recognition, and the elder will start sending orders to his contacts. With a century or 2 in his back, the elder knows a little things about how this lupines behave. He will immediatly phone his ghoul at the police station to tell him to &quot;stay on the alert&quot;, and will have the police divert full resources to investigate a few particular cases.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the elder contacts the remaining eldars and prince, who all start to make preparations. The city Mayor begins to draft new legislation; they are going to sprung a trap for the pesky wolves.<br /> <br /> 7 parks in the city will become sites for mining operations. The eldars expect to dislodge the wolves from their lairs, or if that fails, to lure them to come protect those sites.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the wolves believe this is either something done by humans - or perhaps by wyrm agents. They investigate and the sort of those changes in the city legislation is an entrepreneur ghoul. The trap is sprung. This is too obvious of a target - this MUST be a Wyrm minion. Little do the wolves know, but this is just bait.<br /> <br /> When the wolves come to get their target, the vampires identifty each one of them and follow them to their hidding. Now the vampires' elders circle know who they are and where they are.<br /> <br /> Dont expect those elders to come to fight the wolves with their fists. Hell no. They send high numbers of well armed neonates to hunt the wolves down, one by one and when the wolves are alone, in ambushes.<br /> <br /> In no time, the entire pack is slaughtered. And it only costed a single ghoul.<br /> <br /> Mages control governments (mostly the Technocracy, but anyway), however vampires control local powers. Vampires have the keys to day-to-day power, the one that directly influence all of us.<br /> <br /> A werewolf that scoffs at that power is not long for this world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T19:32:22-07:00","id":1484408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484400#post1484400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf that scoffs at that power is not long for this world.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but for this same reason most don't. One of the most common advice for werewolves about Vampires in the books is about their ability to manipulate things from afar.<br /> <br /> Stating such a scenario with so much detail and predicted outcomes has the problem of stepping beyond the point (control of local powers, which I agree to be an excellent asset) to go into the same mistake of examining shallow scenarios and misrepresentation of the splats. Werewolves are as able of playing smart as vampires, and many of them learn quickly to do it. And Elders are paranoid, they won't go with such a plan without absolute certainty it won't backfire.<br /> <br /> More probably, the werewolves won't ever notice the Neonate in the first place and won't be noticed, either. If they are noticed, the elders or Sabbat higher-ups will be informed and keep tags on the threat, certainly, but at first just waiting for the werewolves to go away or settle. If the werewolves aren't after vampires specifically, they'll eventually leave or become a fixture of some area, and you just adapt accordingly. If they do become a problem, you feed them your enemies and if this isn't enough you make life harder for them through completely mundane channels to convince them to go away. You probably don't need to sacrifice a Ghoul to just find out where they are if you simply have patience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T22:40:04-07:00","id":1484416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484400#post1484400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are not dumb, quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> What the &quot;lone vampire&quot; will do will be to inform his elder about &quot;lupine activity&quot; in the city. The elder will say &quot;thank you&quot;, the neonate will receive some token recognition, and the elder will start sending orders to his contacts. With a century or 2 in his back, the elder knows a little things about how this lupines behave. He will immediatly phone his ghoul at the police station to tell him to &quot;stay on the alert&quot;, and will have the police divert full resources to investigate a few particular cases.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the elder contacts the remaining eldars and prince, who all start to make preparations. The city Mayor begins to draft new legislation; they are going to sprung a trap for the pesky wolves.<br /> <br /> 7 parks in the city will become sites for mining operations. The eldars expect to dislodge the wolves from their lairs, or if that fails, to lure them to come protect those sites.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the wolves believe this is either something done by humans - or perhaps by wyrm agents. They investigate and the sort of those changes in the city legislation is an entrepreneur ghoul. The trap is sprung. This is too obvious of a target - this MUST be a Wyrm minion. Little do the wolves know, but this is just bait.<br /> <br /> When the wolves come to get their target, the vampires identifty each one of them and follow them to their hidding. Now the vampires' elders circle know who they are and where they are.<br /> <br /> Dont expect those elders to come to fight the wolves with their fists. Hell no. They send high numbers of well armed neonates to hunt the wolves down, one by one and when the wolves are alone, in ambushes.<br /> <br /> In no time, the entire pack is slaughtered. And it only costed a single ghoul.<br /> <br /> Mages control governments (mostly the Technocracy, but anyway), however vampires control local powers. Vampires have the keys to day-to-day power, the one that directly influence all of us.<br /> <br /> A werewolf that scoffs at that power is not long for this world.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of &quot;plan&quot; is an awful lot of stirring a hornet's nest for no reason, and contains a few too many moving parts. The bit with the ghoul is also going to clue them in that something weird is going on relative to &quot;normal&quot; corporate shenanigans with monsters, since they're used to Troma mutants coming out of the woodwork. When that doesn't happen, it's going to be concerning, and then you're going to rope in the Garou (or possibly Fera) who know a few things about vampires. Most vampires tend to want to avoid this kind of escalation, because it disrupts their power bases and exposes their machinations. &quot;Extermination&quot;, if done at all, is generally something that they're probably going to take a long view on. Instead of moving in, they're likely to do things little by little to avoid trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T07:11:54-07:00","id":1484421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484416#post1484416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sort of &amp;quot;plan&amp;quot; is an awful lot of stirring a hornet's nest for no reason, and contains a few too many moving parts. The bit with the ghoul is also going to clue them in that something weird is going on relative to &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; corporate shenanigans with monsters, since they're used to Troma mutants coming out of the woodwork. When that doesn't happen, it's going to be concerning, and then you're going to rope in the Garou (or possibly Fera) who know a few things about vampires. Most vampires tend to want to avoid this kind of escalation, because it disrupts their power bases and exposes their machinations. &amp;quot;Extermination&amp;quot;, if done at all, is generally something that they're probably going to take a long view on. Instead of moving in, they're likely to do things little by little to avoid trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was just a silly example, not an in-dept military analyzes of intelligence gathering. It was just to illustrate for some people that think that werewolves can simply claw in and out their way of police officers at will, for instance. It was just to illustrate a point in an easy and quick way.<br /> <br /> Im not going to post a mini book about something that would be an entire adventure in a forum post in order to describe such an event in the needed minutia. You're reading too much into something that is just an over simplification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T07:44:11-07:00","id":1484422,"title":"","content":"And I was answering the girl above who were scoffing at the vampires massive influence. That is a total lack of understanding of what being able to pull strings means.<br /> <br /> Because it means that is FAR easier for the vampires to find out where the pesky wolves are than the other way around. The vampires have jornalists, police, organized crime, basically ALL of the local structure functioning as contacts. What do the wolves have? The kin? Werewolves live isolated from human society and culture. They do not integrate all too well.<br /> <br /> Having all that influence, means vampires have a ton of safe heavens. Not only that, vampires are loners, if you find a heaven of a vampire - congratulations, you managed to get a jump on a single vampire.<br /> <br /> Weres on the other hand go in packs. That's both a strenght and a weakness. Because, once you find were they hide, you find all of them.<br /> <br /> So, just in the field of &quot;scouting&quot; alone, the vamps already have a clear and definitive advantage. What else can they do? What good is &quot;Influence&quot; for?<br /> <br /> Harassment: vampires can set the police against the Garou's family. John may be a big bad wolf, but his sister Suzy is not. She's human. Police can plant drugs on her car, the local DA and the Judge can decide to make an example of her for no apparent reason.<br /> <br /> Jornalists can keep taking their noses into the Garous businesses. Disturbing their activities, spilling secrets to the Garous' enemies. Some players may also scoff at this - until they realize that the local Pentex is using information from tabloids to track their Caern.<br /> <br /> Local crime can be used to harass and even gun down a few parents.<br /> <br /> Local businesses can buy and repurpose propriety sensible to the Garous - not just &quot;the Caern&quot;, this is too narrow of a view to just think in those simplistic terms. There are plenty of changes in a city that can harass, annoy or even become dangerous for the lupines. Changing a school that the lupines used as a base of contacts into a mall or a factory or a parking lot can cause great disrupt into the lupines plans of action.<br /> <br /> Yes, like Monteparnas said, the vamps will probably keep tabs, try to avoid that menace, and if not possible, they'll harass the wolves to try to convince them to move.<br /> <br /> Direct confrontation will only ever come if the lupines are hellbent on causing trouble at all costs.<br /> <br /> If that is the case, eventually the wolves will end up being visited by a massive blood hunt.<br /> <br /> And, like it has already been made clear here, attackers always have the advantage for being prepared for it.<br /> <br /> And, in any scenario, the vamps will ALWAYS be prepared","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T08:14:26-07:00","id":1484423,"title":"","content":"Vampires are pretty subtle about their feeding because they don\u2019t actually have any innate ability to warp the perceptions of witnesses the way the Delirium does. As such, your average werewolf isn\u2019t going to notice them any more than anyone else would unless they have and are actively using gifts to detect them.<br /> <br /> Vampires also take steps to secure their feeding grounds. They don\u2019t just hunt at nightclubs, they OWN the nightclubs and have ghouled bouncers and private rooms they can invite favored patrons to. They worm their way into hospitals, rehab and hospice facilities where a pint here and a pint there from those already ill (and whom they can offer a respite from their suffering through the Kiss) is unlikely to be noticed. Some even open blood donation centers or arrange blood drives (why do the Masons in town hold so many? Because the Tremere backing them need a lot for their Thaumaturgy). Some own apartment complexes where they show up at residents\u2019 doors after dark to do maintenance and are invited in with a tone of relief. Hell, hookup culture turns dating apps into delivery menus for the enterprising vampire (\u201cdo I feel like Mexican or Chinese tonight?\u201d).<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s not like there\u2019s much evidence after the fact unless the vampire was already starving; an intense wave of pleasure as they bite down, a lick to close the wound after and the victim is left a little lightheaded (maybe\u2026 I don\u2019t even notice a difference after I donate at the Red Cross) and replaces that lost pint of blood volume in about 24 hours (what takes longer to recharge are the mineral stores the marrow uses to replace that volume).<br /> <br /> In short, unless you\u2019re actively looking for them via generally supernatural or hi-tech means or the vampire has already screwed up (which letting yourself get to \u201cstarving\u201d most certainly is), your typical werewolf, mummy, mage or hunter just isn\u2019t going to notice that a vampire is even present.<br /> <br /> By the same token it\u2019s not like vampires don\u2019t have their own means of supernatural sensing; Auspex is not a rare discipline and one rank is enough to generally let you know you\u2019re being watched while two ranks just puts a flashing neon sign over any supernaturals in their line of sight while it\u2019s active (and both are generally useful for hunting as locating an isolated target healthy enough to survive feeding and thus not leave any evidence makes your unlife much easier.<br /> <br /> The nocturnal vs. diurnal schedule also makes a big difference. Sure there\u2019s some overlap on the edges, but the human society with which most mages and homid werewolves directly interact is the diurnal world where only a vampire\u2019s proxies are present.<br /> <br /> In short, I just don\u2019t think many splats would encounter each other directly unless they went out of their way to do so. Their proxies? Sure\u2026 probably all the time without even realizing it. The file clerk the mage private investigator has as a contact has no idea her precinct captain is the ghoul of a local vampire or that one of the precinct beat cops is a Bone Gnawer kinfolk or that a barely remembered cold case box is the fetter of a Wraith who died while <i>this</i> close to cracking it.<br /> <br /> But basically each splat has their own particular concerns that only tangentially come close to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 06-19-2022, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T10:23:10-07:00","id":1484430,"title":"","content":"Human weapons&gt; everything. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are weak in the art of &quot;Moar Dakka&quot;. Only a tiny camp of a small tribe understand the appeal of launching metal projectiles with chemical explosions in rapid succession. Mages tend towards the extremes of either &quot;no dakka&quot; or &quot;Dakka+&quot; but generally speaking the &quot;more dakka&quot; mage camp are mostly only able to go for quality and really struggle with quantity. Vampires have massive advantages when it comes to guns: they've got an innate resistance to low level guns, have many low level powers that synergize well with guns and bombs, and they can cheaply field cost-effective ghouls that are superior to humans and they're all too-happy to die with guns. Every single common discipline brings a huge advantage to the table when it comes to modern warfare. <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: Ambushing lone Vampires<br /> I think the <b>Awareness</b> talent would get triggered were lupines or mages move towards ganking vampires, Auspex or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T12:44:36-07:00","id":1484437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484421#post1484421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're reading too much into something that is just an over simplification.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of over simplification does not help exemplify anything, because it comes from wrong assumptions and anyone who notices those assumptions will then disregard everything you tried to say. A lot of the problem here comes exactly from a lot of WoD <u><b>players</b></u> having limited understanding and wrong assumptions about game lines they don't play, so you just reinforce the prejudice of some directly and infuriate the others, making them reinforce their own opposing prejudices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I was answering the girl above who were scoffing at the vampires massive influence. That is a total lack of understanding of what being able to pull strings means.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually it was just lack of interest. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> is one of the experienced Vampire STs in the forums, but mostly a <b>Sabbat ST</b>. That is where the interest in exploring Vampires as lone hunters comes from. That's why I answered avoiding going into the whole &quot;influence&quot; aspect all over again.<br /> <br /> Read that post with care and you'll see that it isn't questioning the effectiveness of influence, but the assumption of this being their necessary role, when their actual necessary role is that of Lone Predator (which has more nuance to it, but is essentially true).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it means that is FAR easier for the vampires to find out where the pesky wolves are than the other way around. The vampires have jornalists, police, organized crime, basically ALL of the local structure functioning as contacts. What do the wolves have? The kin? Werewolves live isolated from human society and culture. They do not integrate all too well.</div> </div> </div> </div>And any actual Werewolf player will disagree with you, because there are a lot of caveats and nuance to this, except where your assumptions are blatantly wrong.<br /> <br /> What I <b>will</b> agree with is that the Vampire's method of influence is more likely to result in early warning than any other, or than trying to use your personal powers to do so. With their <i>collective</i> tentacles in the city and focus on the Masquerade or in unearthing signs of Camarilla invasion, Vampires are the splat most likely to find out about news in the city before everyone else. Truth is, given time, anyone with an interest in the matter will hear about the signs of activity by a given splat, so both Vampires and Werewolves will find about the general presence of one another. But Vampires will <i>probably</i> get it first and be able to get more info in short time without getting personally involved, specially because they will use resources that aren't really threatening to the wolves. The long term thinking also means the typical vampire is more likely to have the kind of mindset necessary to be several moves ahead of the typical werewolf, but that has more to do with mindset and typical individuals than any true advantage or strong cultural aspects, both groups have lots of short-focus imbeciles and mastermind strategists.<br /> <br /> Other than that, while many Kinfolk communities are somewhat isolated and prefer rural and wild areas, integrating with society as a whole is <i><b>their main purpose</b></i>. While it is there, reproduction is actually a secondary role. And they're extremely effective in this role because they play it as a community.<br /> <br /> Many, maybe most Kinfolk communities are reasonably rich and go to great lengths to have at least some key members in really powerful positions in society. They are the trope of powerful but isolated families that control the world while keeping a low profile, at least as a family. Silver Fangs? Some of the richest traditional families in the area are Kinfolk, maybe 1 or 2 members of each legislative house in every level. Shadow Lords? They would literally have tribal schools for teaching advanced lobby practices, and being able to arrange a business meeting with the local Camarilla Prince in equal terms wouldn't be an unreasonable challenge for Ranks 4 or 5. Get of Fenris, Fianna, Black Furies, they're all well connected and wealthy within their national societies. Glass Walkers own big businesses, key corporate and political positions, control criminal cartels. The same tropes the Revenant families go for in VtM and many more are done by Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weres on the other hand go in packs. That's both a strenght and a weakness. Because, once you find were they hide, you find all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never find their whole network. Even if you get a whole Pack, or even a whole Sept, their communications put even the Tremere to shame. The disappearance of a Werewolf is unlikely to go unnoticed or ignored by others, unless they're Ronin. Any Caern isn't only in regular contact with at least some others, through the Moon Bridge they're effectively in walking distance of at least one other, usually more.<br /> <br /> So yeah, they're relatively easy to find, it isn't even meant to be different from that (most Caern locations are open secrets at most). This will hardly change things a lot as they're fortresses, not hideouts, and locating them isn't intended to be the real problem. Their actual secrets are about defenses, layout, allies, scouts, you know, actual warfare capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jornalists can keep taking their noses into the Garous businesses. Disturbing their activities, spilling secrets to the Garous' enemies. Some players may also scoff at this - until they realize that the local Pentex is using information from tabloids to track their Caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an unwinnable situation unless you're moving to open war. Garou aren't dumb, low-key harassment is certainly an option, but learning and leaking their secrets to their enemies will be noticed and dealt with as top priority, since they're a militaristic society and understand pretty well the value of Intel.<br /> <br /> Here's a very good example of how wrong assumptions demonstrate poor understanding of the different games and jeopardize mutual understanding. In Werewolf society any sept leader who doesn't take this stuff seriously enough won't be sept leader for long, and the sept is likely to reach to allies if they don't have the kind of specialists they need to track and deal with the source of all those problems.<br /> <br /> And not only the Wyrm is top suspect, if they can't find clues quickly they'll figure it must be vampires in no time and start to look in the right places with the right tools. They don't understand the intricacies of Kindred society, but they know enough of the general gist of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Local crime can be used to harass and even gun down a few parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that you just said they'll gun down <i>os pais deles</i> instead of <i><u>parentes deles</u></i>?<br /> <br /> You wanted to say Kinfolk. Understandable mistake, false cognates are a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Local businesses can buy and repurpose propriety sensible to the Garous</div> </div> </div> </div>They both play this game, with the sensible difference that Garou property is usually kept &quot;resistant&quot; to hostile takeovers because this is a prime strategy of their usual enemies. If your opposition is primarily Glass Walker, which is usually the case when vampires are concerned, they pretty much specialize in this same game and are keenly aware of which structures in the city are key to their activities.<br /> <br /> If they're Corporate Wolves you're basically going to war with a bunch of Ventrue. Maybe they're even better pals of the local Ventrue than you, so you may very well be going to war with a bunch of Ventrue-like wolves plus the actual Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484422#post1484422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, in any scenario, the vamps will ALWAYS be prepared</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They're both able to prepare and keep intel. And most septs know better than to go to war with the local vampires for no reason, too, despite their general state of open hostility.<br /> <br /> The thing is, neither side is dumb in general and both have stupid members. Both are prone to strategic mistakes. And in open war they'll both end up losing a lot more than they should for little gain, it is bound to be a Pyrrhic victory, and they know that. Vampires will win an open war? If you mean total inter-splat war without cross alliances, then yes, probably, because they have the advantage of stealth and fast replenishment to compensate any direct loss.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean any particular vampire would, except in the sense of winning against fellow vampires, and keep in mind that such a war would probably happen in a specific context where many other things are likely happening, and then everything is up to guess. Werewolves have access to lots of strategies vampires don't, like a literal siege of the city to cut key supplies to their enemies and other actions. They can hunt during daylight, not just vampires, but their Ghouls and Dominated pawns. And they can and will, if the circumstances are dire enough (which won't take much for GW or SL), strike alliances with other vampires. Not even the Get is completely above counting with help of the lesser of two evils.<br /> <br /> -------------------------//-------------------------//-------------------------<br /> <br /> All that is just to say that, again, things are complex, they don't happen in a vacuum. Vampires and werewolves occupy distinct niches and have distinct goals and approaches, but they're also perfectly capable to analyze, learn and adapt. The problem with any physical confrontation is that it already means something went wrong, or at lest weird, and isn't the best way to describe which one is the strongest or something.<br /> <br /> Several years ago we had a series of very interesting threads around here about cross-splat fights using several actual builds and statistical analysis, and the main take away from this was that, despite there being general winners or losers, it's actually very hard to say in a vacuum who'll win a direct confrontation, and everyone is capable of optimized builds to thrash the others, or very bad builds that won't hold their own against many things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484423#post1484423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their proxies? Sure\u2026 probably all the time without even realizing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another interesting aspect to it is that their proxies aren't exactly like them, they're usually more individualistic and autonomous than usually given credit for, and for those reasons they are more likely to work together if the don't have some strong reason to not do so. Depending on the situation, instead of not knowing about each other, those three cops could very well have some inkling and be actually working together to clean some messes and keep info out of the public's eyes, with the closeness of the relationship depending both on themselves and on their roles for their supernatural patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T14:47:31-07:00","id":1484442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484437#post1484437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an unwinnable situation unless you're moving to open war. Garou aren't dumb, low-key harassment is certainly an option, but learning and leaking their secrets to their enemies will be noticed and dealt with as top priority, since they're a militaristic society and understand pretty well the value of Intel.<br /> <br /> Here's a very good example of how wrong assumptions demonstrate poor understanding of the different games and jeopardize mutual understanding. In Werewolf society any sept leader who doesn't take this stuff seriously enough won't be sept leader for long, and the sept is likely to reach to allies if they don't have the kind of specialists they need to track and deal with the source of all those problems.<br /> <br /> And not only the Wyrm is top suspect, if they can't find clues quickly they'll figure it must be vampires in no time and start to look in the right places with the right tools. They don't understand the intricacies of Kindred society, but they know enough of the general gist of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the assumption being made is about the endless cross splats &quot;battle royales&quot;, so yeah, this would be a near war situation.<br /> <br /> I agree with you. That kind of stuff is NOT common AT ALL. It would be a total exception. Which is why it would be a massive pain for both sides, which is why both will try to avoid it as much as possible.<br /> <br /> This situation would be the result of dumb weres doing dumb shit. But it's the same as dumb neonates managing to get in trouble with the wolves. Those are exceptions. And whichever side has dumb individuals doing dumbery stuff, those will undoubtly pay the price.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484437#post1484437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware that you just said they'll gun down <i>os pais deles</i> instead of <i><u>parentes deles</u></i>?<br /> <br /> You wanted to say Kinfolk. Understandable mistake, false cognates are a pain in the ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaarrgh I always forget that &quot;parents&quot; in english is only mother and father and not relatives. &quot;Parentes&quot; is relatives in portuguese. Dumb mistake, dumb dumb bah!<br /> <br /> How do you know that? Are you brazilian too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T15:14:56-07:00","id":1484444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484430#post1484430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human weapons&gt; everything.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are weak in the art of &quot;Moar Dakka&quot;. Only a tiny camp of a small tribe understand the appeal of launching metal projectiles with chemical explosions in rapid succession. Mages tend towards the extremes of either &quot;no dakka&quot; or &quot;Dakka+&quot; but generally speaking the &quot;more dakka&quot; mage camp are mostly only able to go for quality and really struggle with quantity. Vampires have massive advantages when it comes to guns: they've got an innate resistance to low level guns, have many low level powers that synergize well with guns and bombs, and they can cheaply field cost-effective ghouls that are superior to humans and they're all too-happy to die with guns. Every single common discipline brings a huge advantage to the table when it comes to modern warfare.<br /> <br /> <br /> RE: Ambushing lone Vampires<br /> I think the <b>Awareness</b> talent would get triggered were lupines or mages move towards ganking vampires, Auspex or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the Garou a bit off on guns. Aside from the anomalous placement of the V2e PG, the other place where support and vehicle weapons showed up was War of the Amazon, where everyone who was comfortable with human form was probably toting an assault rifle and grenades. This is also how the conflict is depicted in the opening comic for Bastet - while the lupus packmate isn't packing heat, the other two presumable human-born packmates are, and even the werejaguar narrator is in on the action, with an assault rifle and grenades for when having the venerable Mokole Breath of Fire as an ally isn't the the card to play just yet.<br /> <br /> Away from that conflict, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers in their entirety are likely to pick up and use guns, because they're already sus to the rest of the GN and so suffer no hits to renown. Most GW Gifts that have to do with guns are also general use - the Dies Ultimae Gift lore generally concentrates on other aspects of modern warfare, such as communication and getting cover to fire from. Garafena's Crown means infinite dakka for the scene, such that fire has to be moderated to avoid damaging the gun. I also wouldn't describe the Soldiers or the Glass Walkers as tiny or small relative to other camps and tribes, either; GWs are one of the contenders for the most populous Gaian tribes, and the Dies Ultimae have a literal cult following given all of the end times rhetoric.<br /> <br /> As an archaic side capability, some Garou pursue bows as dakka, and the Black Furies are infamous for ensuring that you'll fight in the shade. Of course, when what's raining down are talen arrows that burst into flames, that's a pretty effective incendiary attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T16:24:35-07:00","id":1484450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484444#post1484444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an archaic side capability, some Garou pursue bows as dakka, and the Black Furies are infamous for ensuring that you'll fight in the shade. Of course, when what's raining down are talen arrows that burst into flames, that's a pretty effective incendiary attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very relevant point for the &quot;moar dakka&quot; side of things. As a rule of thumb Werewolf is the second splat with more easy access to &quot;magic items&quot; as Fetishes and Talens. Even if you don't have personal toys in your character sheet, they have an extremely easy time making new items even compared to Mages. They're only behind Changelings in this regard.<br /> <br /> And in the end, yes, just being able to put your hands on a lot of guns and ammunition is quite effective against any splat. It is also quite simple for anyone to pull out if they want to go all-out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T00:07:23-07:00","id":1484481,"title":"","content":"Because 1) Vampires are more numerous and thus more expendable from a writter perspective and 2) As other splats are less numerous from game design perspective they need more strengh not to be predated upon. Quick reprodution is part of why the vampire race is so succesful and one of his strengh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T01:05:15-07:00","id":1484484,"title":"","content":"From what I know Baba Yaga exterminated a third of the Garou of Russia and had she not been killed (not by a werewolf, moreover) the situation would have been even more tragic.<br /> <br /> Basically the vampires will always try not to fight the Garou openly, they just need an eviction notice, a few ghouls and cameras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T03:35:58-07:00","id":1484495,"title":"","content":"Baba Yaga was a great example what could happen when some ancient with her caliber decide, to actually <i>act</i> not just sit around twiddling her thumbs... she steamrolled a good portion of the word and sealed it away. And basically no sept, no technoracy, no one been able to do anything, the story needed a litral stupid deux ex machina, Vasilisa to &quot;kill&quot; her. I used &quot;kill&quot; because some later supplements like Lore of the Clans and Beckett's jyhad diary toyed the idea, she might just retreted back to the shadow and the whole Vasilisa-act was just a nice trick.<br /> Anyhow, her reign was handled horribly, I mean it's end, by all accounts Baba Yaga's return and the fact she showed the world how to carve out a portion from it, should have been a signal for the others and in a few months (ot be generous, years) WoD shouls have been transformed a quasi post-apocaliptic survival game, where Blood Gods rule over wast territories, openly untill Caine decides to show up and the guano hit the fanning slave.<br /> Obviously, since V:TM is/was a gothic personal horror game wiht social aspect, this couldn't happen<br /> But showed what could happen if such monsters like Baba Yaga, Mithras, ur-Shulgi, Meneleus, Odin, Helena, Nebmaatsutekh (not a widly known Settite ancient, but when Nebmaatsutekh awakened from torpor during the Dark Ages she proved that the legend was real about Sutekh fighting for Ra against Apep and the Sun God still owns a favor for it... proved by the fact, invocing this ancient pact, she was able to withstand the sunlight for an entire day.) Montano, the Malkavian Word-Eater (or even Nissiku), Hazimel, the Rakshasa of Rakshasas or Kartarirya suddenly decides... okay, enough! The World is OURS...<br /> It wasn't pretty<br /> When Baba Yaga swept away septs of Garou, I think the Shadow Lords had a collective PTSD from it, remembering the time when the Tzimisce Antediluvian with its chilren handed their furry behind to them, freed Kupala and forced them to share their ancestral home with the Fiends. (and basically they never evicted the Tzimisce... quite the opposite, in the past ten thousand years they developed a love hate relationship as room mates)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-20-2022, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T06:19:05-07:00","id":1484505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484484#post1484484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I know Baba Yaga exterminated a third of the Garou of Russia and had she not been killed (not by a werewolf, moreover) the situation would have been even more tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the actions of a Methuselah account for much in the spirit of the thread. They're the exception of vampire society, not what you're usually seeing on the streets, much less in the depictions cited in the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484495#post1484495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga was a great example what could happen when some ancient with her caliber decide, to actually <i>act</i> not just sit around twiddling her thumbs...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I don't think she was a great example of anything.<br /> <br /> First, the whole Iron Curtain was a terrible idea, in-game and out-of-game. Out, it alienated Soviet (in the geographical sense) players and made a huge chunk of the world inaccessible for reasons. It was a continuation of the Cold War after its end just because most of the American writers at the time didn't knew better, they had no idea on how to depict Russia at all without the lenses of the regime (and maybe didn't wanted to show that it's transition from Socialism was actually a huge political and economic crisis). In-game it just made no sense, never got a reasonable explanation (Baba Yaga wasn't one) and had no apparent consequence to the rest of the world nor got any attention despite being literally a sixth of the total dry land on Earth and bigger in both area and population than the US and Canada combined.<br /> <br /> Then her demise was.. deplorable. It was among the dumbest tales in WoD's publication history, and that isn't a small feat. Railroaded, deus-ex-machina, bland characters, references pulled from a well-known folktale without anything that really resembled the folktale except the creature deciding to appear to the players as the girl just 'cause. Badly written in every conceivable way, but it was urgently needed because at the time they noticed they really had to get rid of the stupid Iron Curtain A.S.A.P..<br /> <br /> Her reign shouldn't have kick-started the apocalyptic world, it should have attracted the combined fury of so many other big players in the stage on her head. The only thing she gained was a big red target, and with everything other splats can pull out under extreme pressure, I don't buy that she had such a thorough control over the Silver Fangs in their own turf while behaving like a deluded maniac.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the setting, not even the literal awakening of Ravnos, ever had the sheer power and span of what she did, yet she didn't show any ability, skill, insight or behavior that could lend credibility to such a feat, and ended up dying an ignominious death in Russia: The Exposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T07:12:08-07:00","id":1484509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484444#post1484444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Away from that conflict, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers in their entirety are likely to pick up and use guns, because they're already sus to the rest of the GN and so suffer no hits to renown. Most GW Gifts that have to do with guns are also general use - the Dies Ultimae Gift lore generally concentrates on other aspects of modern warfare, such as communication and getting cover to fire from. Garafena's Crown means infinite dakka for the scene, such that fire has to be moderated to avoid damaging the gun. I also wouldn't describe the Soldiers or the Glass Walkers as tiny or small relative to other camps and tribes, either; GWs are one of the contenders for the most populous Gaian tribes, and the Dies Ultimae have a literal cult following given all of the end times rhetoric.<br /> <br /> As an archaic side capability, some Garou pursue bows as dakka, and the Black Furies are infamous for ensuring that you'll fight in the shade. Of course, when what's raining down are talen arrows that burst into flames, that's a pretty effective incendiary attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>-Garou in the Amazon are notably weird to most of the Garou nation. IDK 'bout you but the werewolves in the amazon stuff comes off as significantly more tongue-in-cheek than the usual werewolf eco-terrorism.<br /> -Bone Gnawers aren't likely to pick up guns that are worth anything. Guns are more a tool of convenience/adaptation to American cities rather than as serious means of warfare against the Wyrm.<br /> -Glass walkers <i>are</i> one of the smaller tribes. One with a barely functional wolf population and larger than average metis numbers. Are they the smallest? Probably not. But I'll laugh you out of the room if you think they can compete with the BSD, BG, F, Uk or CoG for numbers. If your definition of &quot;one of the most populous Gaian tribes&quot; is being placed at 5th or 6th out of 12 then I can't chide you too much but I'd argue that the difference between each tribes size is pretty big and the top 3 are probably bigger individually than the bottom 6 combined.<br /> <br /> Guns&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Bows.<br /> Otherwise we wouldn't have made the switch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-20-2022, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T09:18:24-07:00","id":1484515,"title":"","content":"I figure vampires deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T09:59:37-07:00","id":1484517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484509#post1484509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Garou in the Amazon are notably weird to most of the Garou nation. IDK 'bout you but the werewolves in the amazon stuff comes off as significantly more tongue-in-cheek than the usual werewolf eco-terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that weird, really, because they didn't seem to have an insurmountable issue hopping to it when it was necessary. Also, that sounds like a personal problem, as I spend my days contemplating how to use A Time of War as a substitute for the Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Bone Gnawers aren't likely to pick up guns that are worth anything. Guns are more a tool of convenience/adaptation to American cities rather than as serious means of warfare against the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>That's a really weird conclusion. They might not have a lot of them at hand, but if they need them, they probably know where to get them. Likely, from the same place that the more militant Ratkin acquire them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Glass walkers <i>are</i> one of the smaller tribes. One with a barely functional wolf population and larger than average metis numbers. Are they the smallest? Probably not. But I'll laugh you out of the room if you think they can compete with the BSD, BG, F, Uk or CoG for numbers. If your definition of &quot;one of the most populous Gaian tribes&quot; is being placed at 5th or 6th out of 12 then I can't chide you too much but I'd argue that the difference between each tribes size is pretty big and the top 3 are probably bigger individually than the bottom 6 combined. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Revised Storyteller's Handbook, page 35, lists the GWs as one of the larger tribes; I'm not entirely sure that order has much to do with it (the Silver Fangs usually seem like they're supposed to be rare but come up just after the GWs), but they're in the middle. The small ones are the Furies, the Striders, the Stargazers (somehow), and the Talons. It's quite baffling to suggest that the GWs are a tiny, niche tribe when their turf is the city and they range over most major cities of many of the most populous countries in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guns&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;Bows.<br /> Otherwise we wouldn't have made the switch. </div> </div> </div>Magic doesn't exist, either. If you have a magic bow and a magic gun, it might not matter so much, especially if you can make the engagement area burst into flames with the former but not so much the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-20-2022, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T10:01:30-07:00","id":1484518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484515#post1484515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure vampires deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate. No one likes vampires - not even other vampires!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T11:12:18-07:00","id":1484521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484515#post1484515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure vampires deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh they most definitely do but don't think that the other splats are any better, werewolves in particular are in some ways even worse than vamps and let's not even get into mages, the only ones who could be considered somewhat better are probably changelings and I bet they do plenty of fucked up shit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T11:43:58-07:00","id":1484526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484450#post1484450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very relevant point for the &amp;quot;moar dakka&amp;quot; side of things. As a rule of thumb Werewolf is the second splat with more easy access to &amp;quot;magic items&amp;quot; as Fetishes and Talens. Even if you don't have personal toys in your character sheet, they have an extremely easy time making new items even compared to Mages. They're only behind Changelings in this regard.<br /> <br /> And in the end, yes, just being able to put your hands on a lot of guns and ammunition is quite effective against any splat. It is also quite simple for anyone to pull out if they want to go all-out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Mages MASS PRODUCE the magical mojo. That's why they have Hit Marks and Victors and Ciborgs and Golems. No, no splat outproduces Mages in terms of &quot;magic industry&quot;. Also, Mages stablish &quot;shared factories&quot;. They can each produce one part of the &quot;mojo&quot;. You dont need every Mage to have Prime 4-5 or Spirit 4-5 for their &quot;factories&quot; (Im putting factories under quotations here, but sometimes it's actually literal). You can have one &quot;mutant super being&quot; being &quot;modeled&quot; by one Mage with Life 5, while another one toy with it using Entropy 4, yet another makes improvements using Mind 1-5 and a forth do it using Prime 5.<br /> <br /> No other splat can do that. And that's why despite being the less numerous splat they puch so above their weight, it's because they can simply take Joe Shmoe from the streets and turn him into a killing machine. No other splat have such a capacity to condense their supernatural mojo in an external source that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:04:22-07:00","id":1484529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484505#post1484505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the actions of a Methuselah account for much in the spirit of the thread. They're the exception of vampire society, not what you're usually seeing on the streets, much less in the depictions cited in the OP.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually I don't think she was a great example of anything.<br /> <br /> First, the whole Iron Curtain was a terrible idea, in-game and out-of-game. Out, it alienated Soviet (in the geographical sense) players and made a huge chunk of the world inaccessible for reasons. It was a continuation of the Cold War after its end just because most of the American writers at the time didn't knew better, they had no idea on how to depict Russia at all without the lenses of the regime (and maybe didn't wanted to show that it's transition from Socialism was actually a huge political and economic crisis). In-game it just made no sense, never got a reasonable explanation (Baba Yaga wasn't one) and had no apparent consequence to the rest of the world nor got any attention despite being literally a sixth of the total dry land on Earth and bigger in both area and population than the US and Canada combined.<br /> <br /> Then her demise was.. deplorable. It was among the dumbest tales in WoD's publication history, and that isn't a small feat. Railroaded, deus-ex-machina, bland characters, references pulled from a well-known folktale without anything that really resembled the folktale except the creature deciding to appear to the players as the girl just 'cause. Badly written in every conceivable way, but it was urgently needed because at the time they noticed they really had to get rid of the stupid Iron Curtain A.S.A.P..<br /> <br /> Her reign shouldn't have kick-started the apocalyptic world, it should have attracted the combined fury of so many other big players in the stage on her head. The only thing she gained was a big red target, and with everything other splats can pull out under extreme pressure, I don't buy that she had such a thorough control over the Silver Fangs in their own turf while behaving like a deluded maniac.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the setting, not even the literal awakening of Ravnos, ever had the sheer power and span of what she did, yet she didn't show any ability, skill, insight or behavior that could lend credibility to such a feat, and ended up dying an ignominious death in Russia: The Exposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I personally dislike so much those meta stories about the methusas and antis - or any other big &quot;supers&quot;. It just boils down to &quot;superman vs apokolipse&quot; and more, more, more! &quot;Look how could, the Ravnos ravaging everything and nothing can stop it! So... How do we stop it! Oh I know, nukes! Oh no, not dead! More, more, more! More magic superpowers! Oh yeah, finally dead... But wait! Because here's a brand new book and.. Tandam! Not dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> Is just stupid. It's like the old problem of comics to keep pumping up powers, because you need more powerful villains to challenge the heroes, instead of making INTELLIGENT stories, so now the villain is too powerful, so the heroes need to be even more powerful, but now the heroes are too powerful to be challenged, and you increase the villains even more...<br /> <br /> And that's how you end up with ridiculous things like Thor blowing up Black Holes or Goku almost destroying the universe just by &quot;warming up&quot; his Chi and other such boring nonsense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:11:29-07:00","id":1484532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484509#post1484509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Garou in the Amazon are notably weird to most of the Garou nation. IDK 'bout you but the werewolves in the amazon stuff comes off as significantly more tongue-in-cheek than the usual werewolf eco-terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a brazilian such as myself, that sort of cartoonish depiction of what Amazonia is hilarious. But it doesnt bother me at all, pretty much the entire world that doesnt live in Amazonia have a distorted view of it - including most brazilians and other south americans that have a portion of their territories in the florest.<br /> <br /> To begin with, living in the florest aint an untouched paradise. It's a green hellhole. I always joke and say that if Brazil ever turned totalitarian, our gulags would be at the Amazon, where people would work to death breaking stones and, unlike Siberia, would be a hot and wet hell.<br /> <br /> Also, wolves in south america are pretty much non existant. We have only the Lobo Guar\u00e1 (Guar\u00e1 Wolf). There should be a lot more Bastet here than Garou, since the population of Jaguars, althought small, is significantly bigger than the dwindling local species of wolves.<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, my grand-grandmother once killed a Jaguar. She thought it was a wild dog attacking her chickens, and killed it with a club.<br /> <br /> It was in the night. When she woke up in the morning to dispose of the &quot;dog&quot;, she almost passed out.<br /> <br /> I also knew a biology teacher from another university that was attacked by one. He never saw it coming. He were luck to survive, and have insane scars in his chest. He only survived because he received immediate medical care. I single claw ZAP! It cut his chest open.<br /> <br /> Im scared to death of jaguars, if I ever see one in the open I would shit myself entirely. But probably I would NOT see it - and I would just be dead, just like that.<br /> <br /> But since I live in a big city, there's zero chance of it ever happening. But when travelling in the woods here... I never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-20-2022, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:19:15-07:00","id":1484534,"title":"","content":"Well I assume it's only supposed to be a paradise from a werewolf perspective. Mind you, even that's dubious because wolves are designed for dry forests in cool to cold climates. Do wolves even live in the Amazon? It seems rather hot and wet for creatures designed to thrive in dry, cool-to-cold climates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:26:12-07:00","id":1484535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484521#post1484521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh they most definitely do but don't think that the other splats are any better, werewolves in particular are in some ways even worse than vamps and let's not even get into mages, the only ones who could be considered somewhat better are probably changelings and I bet they do plenty of fucked up shit too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, what's wrong with Mages?<br /> <br /> We are good guys, honestly!<br /> <br /> Now, I'll have to ask you to direct yourself to our &quot;educational&quot; room. It's just down the corridor, number 101, you cannot miss it. Im sure you'll change your mind and see things as they TRULY are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:48:05-07:00","id":1484538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484534#post1484534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I assume it's only supposed to be a paradise from a werewolf perspective. Mind you, even that's dubious because wolves are designed for dry forests in cool to cold climates. Do wolves even live in the Amazon? It seems rather hot and wet for creatures designed to thrive in dry, cool-to-cold climates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brazil has 7 different biomes (depending on who you ask), it aint all just the Amazonic rainforest, and 95% of brazilians actually live as far away from the Amazon as California from Texas almost. One such biome is the &quot;Mata Atlantica&quot; (or &quot;Atlantic Woods&quot; in a very literal translation) which runs from north to south close to the sea in the east. In the middle you have the &quot;Cerrado&quot;, yet another biome. In those areas we have a few representatives of the &quot;Lobo Guar\u00e1&quot;, which is the only species of wolves in South America, with very few numbers. This wolve however is VERY different from both the european or north american versions, and looks more like a big skinny fox than a proper wolf, but it is a &quot;Canis&quot; still, nothing to do with foxeses besides the weird looks. Beautiful beast by the way, I saw it in the zoo and it's a majestic animal.<br /> <br /> They dont live in the Amazon thou, they live in the Cerrado and Mata Atlantica, which are some hundreds to thousands of miles to the south and southeast of Amazon respectively (the Amazon occupies the Northern portions of Brazil and the South of Colombia and Venezuela mainly).<br /> <br /> So yeah... Werewolves in the Amazon makes no sense. They could MAYBE be here in Sao Paulo or Rio de Janeiro, who are cities that exist in the Mata Atlantica biome (no, we dont have forests in our cities, just small fragments of preserved zones, althought we eventually reach the Atlantic Forest if we travel some dozens of miles away from the cities), but Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro, our 2 biggest cities, are thousands of miles removed from the Amazon.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Amazon rainforest aint a single biome either, it's actually 6 different biomes. Sorry, Im an evolutionary biologist, so those subjects aways make my eyes shine. The Amazon up until the holocen was like the African Savanna, thus it was semi-arid. This means that it had 6 different florest in that region, seggregated by semi deserts. When the holocen began however, the region became super wet, so this 6 distinct forest grew and grew and grew... Until they connected.<br /> <br /> There are clear biological distinctions between those by the way, even if they arent visible by any geographical mark. There are plenty of species of plants and animals that DO NOT cross those invisible borders AT ALL. For this reason, there are some types of monkeys you'll only find in one place of the forest, several types of plants that only grow in one portion of it and on and on. It's a truly fascinating place - at least for a biologist lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T13:02:13-07:00","id":1484539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484535#post1484535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, what's wrong with Mages?<br /> <br /> We are good guys, honestly!<br /> <br /> Now, I'll have to ask you to direct yourself to our &quot;educational&quot; room. It's just down the corridor, number 101, you cannot miss it. Im sure you'll change your mind and see things as they TRULY are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;It's a sin, IT'S A SIN&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T13:24:40-07:00","id":1484542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484532#post1484532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a brazilian such as myself, that sort of cartoonish depiction of what Amazonia is hilarious. But it doesnt bother me at all, pretty much the entire world that doesnt live in Amazonia have a distorted view of it - including most brazilians and other south americans that have a portion of their territories in the florest.<br /> <br /> To begin with, living in the florest aint an untouched paradise. It's a green hellhole. I always joke and say that if Brazil ever turned totalitarian, our gulags would be at the Amazon, where people would work to death breaking stones and, unlike Siberia, would be a hot and wet hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD also has old growth forests in Europe and secret packs of Japanese wolves. Rest assured, the entire world is bonkers so that it can be spooky and goffic. Time will tell if the 5th edition games change it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, wolves in south america are pretty much non existant. We have only the Lobo Guar\u00e1 (Guar\u00e1 Wolf). There should be a lot more Bastet here than Garou, since the population of Jaguars, althought small, is significantly bigger than the dwindling local species of wolves. </div> </div> </div>Almost all of the Garou in the region are tourists, basically. That's why the Fera of the region told them to GTFO after they dislodged the particular corp that was looking to expand there, and they had to make good on it or risk getting into another fight against their allies of the moment. The Fera in question being mostly the werejaguars and werecaimans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> rr... Mages MASS PRODUCE the magical mojo. That's why they have Hit Marks and Victors and Ciborgs and Golems. No, no splat outproduces Mages in terms of &quot;magic industry&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The thing about &quot;industry&quot; is that it can end up bricked from a fairly simple Gift. Like, an experienced Ragabash can stop a HIT Mark in its tracks with Jam Technology (disable the computer, it can no longer move) and then move in with Gremlins to finish the job (all electronics in the cyborg are now bricked and have to be replaced, which probably isn't good for the biological components attached to the life support functions). And that's before you get to all the problems with paradox that fetishes don't have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Mages stablish &quot;shared factories&quot;. They can each produce one part of the &quot;mojo&quot;. You dont need every Mage to have Prime 4-5 or Spirit 4-5 for their &quot;factories&quot; (Im putting factories under quotations here, but sometimes it's actually literal). You can have one &quot;mutant super being&quot; being &quot;modeled&quot; by one Mage with Life 5, while another one toy with it using Entropy 4, yet another makes improvements using Mind 1-5 and a forth do it using Prime 5.<br /> <br /> No other splat can do that. And that's why despite being the less numerous splat they puch so above their weight, it's because they can simply take Joe Shmoe from the streets and turn him into a killing machine. No other splat have such a capacity to condense their supernatural mojo in an external source that way. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but when it comes to one-shot objects, Garou and Fera only need a single, one-dot rite and some cooperation from spirits to make many talens. Such as the slagger, a cartoonish fire icon on a button that acts a lot like thermite when activated. It's great for industrial sabotage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-20-2022, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T16:06:57-07:00","id":1484556,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> said, because of mass production and industry, no one has easier access to magical items than *Technocrats (not mages in general). So much so that it's not only narratively appropiate to have them in spades whenever seriously needed (as could be in Werewolf), but you even have a Background that can be used to ask for basically anything, from any kind of &quot;personal weapon&quot; imaginable to a starship armed with magical missiles and bombs, for no other reason than you having the carpet.<br /> <br /> You DO need to return it, or will loose the privilege. But, still, it's pretty insane<i>, </i>especially when that goes along with the usual Background for owning a Wonder, and the one to have one implanted, AND yet another one that allows you to &quot;take&quot; experimental/dangerous stuff, because NWO thinks of you as a test subject..<i>.it's as if Character Sheets were trying to tell us something</i><br /> <br /> However, it's not quite true that other splats can't &quot;externalize&quot; their powers efficiently. I would think this superiority of the Technocracy is not so much because of &quot;inherent RAW potential&quot; as it's because that's &quot;what they do&quot;. It wasn't easy for them, but they went the mile and made it happen, so to speak. Much like how Nosferatu are good at intel not so much because they're the best vampire spies RAW, but because they have the best &quot;clan culture&quot; to make an information network happen, and have built the infraestructure to make it happen.<br /> <br /> This narrative element it's very important, and often overlook. It's not unimaginable that other splats could've done similar or even better in a different setting, maybe if they had different agendas or culture. But for X or Y, it never happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-20-2022, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T22:15:06-07:00","id":1484578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484521#post1484521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh they most definitely do but don't think that the other splats are any better, werewolves in particular are in some ways even worse than vamps and let's not even get into mages, the only ones who could be considered somewhat better are probably changelings and I bet they do plenty of fucked up shit too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings can be more fucked-up than others by far. A child-eating cannibal is perfectly valid as a concept for a starting character that faces almost no repercussion from either game rules or fae society, and kidnapping people for giggles is common practice. All that before even starting to consider their actions as emotional parasites.<br /> <br /> They can be really good if they want and help human society as a whole. But they have no requirement to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484526#post1484526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... Mages MASS PRODUCE the magical mojo.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484556#post1484556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> said, because of mass production and industry, no one has easier access to magical items than *Technocrats (not mages in general).</div> </div> </div> </div>Standard rule for Wonder creation: you need a reasonable level of Prime, which also requires a reasonable Arete to begin with, and at least 1 Quint. With enough Spirit you can try to make a Fetish instead. Installations and organizations that help to improve output exist, but they're not the baseline. And to the point of mass production, only the Technocracy achieves that and even then is mass production in relative terms, not absolute ones.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this isn't good, but there's at least three splats capable of outperforming them:<ul><li>Werewolves create Fetishes with a level 3 Rite, which means just buying 3 dots at an Ability and performing a ritual half an hour long. While there are some complications, a specialized Fetish creator easily outperforms the output of any Union factory in the Earth. What limits them is that such dedicated creators are rare, and Horizon factories can have enough Mages and juice to outpace them, but that's literally by putting more Splat members to do what the Garou have one person doing. Talens and low level Fetishes <b><u>are</u></b> more common and cheaper than Union's Equipment, although the Nation doesn't have the global logistics to deliver it from Caern to Caern in short notice, something the Union can do to make it seems like they have more;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Demons with the Lore of the Forge have an easier time than Mages. It is cheaper to acquire than the Spheres requirements, and generally faster and simpler. Level 1 is enough to permanently reduce the difficulty of using an item, like a weapon, with a touch, a roll and a WP point, and level 3 let you turn raw materials into the desired object with a thought, accelerating the process considerably, and that makes their output with level 4 (actual enchanted items) limited only by their Faith points in speed. So a single Fallen is potentially able to enter a shed with rusted steel tubes and come out half an hour later with half a dozen Dif 3 to hit Enchanted assault rifles;<br /> \u200b</li> <li>Changelings are the single most productive splat. Chimerical Items are frequently more powerful than mundane counterparts and a Changeling has several ways to get one, including it often appearing spontaneously. In the Dreaming or in a Freehold basically anything they craft will be a Chimerical item no matter what, despite being worked upon through completely mundane skills and no special cost. A Freehold that operates as a factory or a factory located in the Dreaming will have standard output for a similar factory, but churning out chimerical items that, while technically not being their actual magical items (those are Treasures), can still have fantastic abilities all the same (life flaming swords). And if they want to make Treasures, there's simply <i>no requirement at all</i> beyond the Art to be imbued. It either takes exquisite and rare components and a mundane craft, or a suitable item to be imbued and some time making rolls and giving it a few Glamour points.<br /> \u200b</li> </ul><br /> <br /> While the Technocratic Union has the mass production of Wonders as one of their main assets and an excellent organization to make the best of it, in the end they don't outperform those splats without putting out a lot of effort, and even them the result is relative, as for those splats the items in question are even seen as relatively trivial in comparison to what a Wonder is in Mage (regardless of them all having the exact same cost in a starting character sheet: Background dots). What the Union really has as an advantage is a very good system to deliver items from place to place, so their already reasonable output is employed all over the place without issue and without useful items resting unused in shelves for decades at a time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484532#post1484532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, wolves in south america are pretty much non existant. We have only the Lobo Guar\u00e1 (Guar\u00e1 Wolf). There should be a lot more Bastet here than Garou, since the population of Jaguars, althought small, is significantly bigger than the dwindling local species of wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do have my own reservations about the whole Amazon War in Werewolf, they're not that dumb.<br /> <br /> The Garou in the war are foreigners that got wind of a Pentex project in the area, and other than then the local Fera are species that do live in the rainforest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484534#post1484534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I assume it's only supposed to be a paradise from a werewolf perspective. Mind you, even that's dubious because wolves are designed for dry forests in cool to cold climates. Do wolves even live in the Amazon? It seems rather hot and wet for creatures designed to thrive in dry, cool-to-cold climates.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cerrado is savanna-like with mostly dry climate and fluctuating temperatures that resemble a temperate climate without freezing winters, so not as bad for wolf-ish animals.<br /> <br /> But even though we have more of them here, you'll hardly see a Lobo-Guar\u00e1 in the open because they're extremely reclusive and wary of humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484538#post1484538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it is a &quot;Canis&quot; still, nothing to do with foxeses besides the weird looks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to doubt if you hold this, but are you sure they're that close to wolves?<br /> <br /> AFAIK They're canini, but not in the <i>Canis</i> genus, so they would be as close as some foxes from the <i>Canini</i> clade (not usual <i>Vulpini </i>foxes, though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T07:11:01-07:00","id":1484604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484578#post1484578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK They're canini, but not in the <i>Canis</i> genus, so they would be as close as some foxes from the <i>Canini</i> clade (not usual <i>Vulpini </i>foxes, though).</div> </div> </div> </div>Chrysocyon brachyurus<br /> <br /> Indeed they are not canis, I just looked it up. It's because the genus also begins with a C, so it gives C.brachyurus which I always assumed to be Canis. <br /> <br /> It's the only member of the genus, so that means it is neither a wolf nor a fox, althought looking like a weird mix of both.<br /> <br /> So there you have it, no wolves in south america at all. Thou werewolves and werefoxes are welcomed to try some weird kinky shit with those guys...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T12:24:19-07:00","id":1484639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Standard rule for Wonder creation: you need a reasonable level of Prime, which also requires a reasonable Arete to begin with, and at least 1 Quint. With enough Spirit you can try to make a Fetish instead. Installations and organizations that help to improve output exist, but they're not the baseline. And to the point of mass production, only the Technocracy achieves that and even then is mass production in relative terms, not absolute ones.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that this isn't good, but there's at least three splats capable of outperforming them</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree in that they're cappable, I'm just saying that they just don't seem to do it. They have their reasons.<br /> <br /> Agreed that the Changelings *do* if you count Chimerical stuff as Wonders (BTW . I don't think you should count ALL Chimerical Socks as Wonders. I'm not even going to comment on turning Freeholds into Factories because I don't want to enter a debate about Banality on a thread that's about <i>Vampires</i> sucking :P - suffice to say<i>this isn't how Changelings opperate normaly.</i>)<br /> <br /> But those notions you have about Wonders are somewhat off, and could be misleading when talking about the Technocracy. All that's presented as a problem there isn't for them, and some of it isn't for average mages either.<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0. If we're going to count &quot;buffed&quot; items as Wonders. That doesn't require Prime, that's just casting a Matter (or appropiate) spell onto something or a bunch of somethings.No need for special instalations for that one, albeit, I guess having them would help. Rules may vary, and I'm not saying a Demon or Changeling have a harder time, they don't: but large scale production of such things a <i>Traditionalist</i> *can* do, too - albeit within hours instead of minutes.<br /> <br /> What trully keeps mages down on this end it's more the general concepts of Paradox, Paradigm, and how &quot;changing the world should be hard&quot;, than the other rules of magick about buffing stuff. And even then, I'm being generous with your argument because...<br /> <br /> Depending on the Lore, and using that\u200b vague sense of &quot;better than normal stuff&quot; to define Wonder, that you're using (which, I think, it's wrong), the only reason everything humans use isn't a magick-fueled wonder it's because when a new introduced technology it's proven better than an old one, it becomming commonplace it's moving the goalpost :P If every big innovation (like, say, how &quot;guns&quot; used to be magick) it's magick, then there's a lot of it - perhaps even ALL of it (hey, I'm not the one that placed impersonal forces like &quot;the Dreaming&quot; as the production of one Splat).<br /> <br /> But, even being generous not counting Mage problematic Lore and weird outliers (like the &quot;Technocratic&quot; weapons and explosives of M20, wtf are those? I guess they <i>could </i>be Trinkets...that follow no magick rule and aren't regarded as magickal at all?) it's still, wrong to use those Wonder rules for something so trivial as making stuff sligthly better than normal. That's what the Trinket's rules are for (and, even then, that's for permanent buffs)<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0 Quintessence it's a limit. But, for the Technocracy, RAW, it's rather on the plentifull end. This due to the rules to obtain it being varied, some on the vage end of things, coupled with them not needing to hidde. So much so that we often have to think reasons for <i>why</i> would they need more of it, least them taking Nodes (while already having some of the biggest), sacrificing mundanes at their job, sucking the Quint from imprisioned mages, taking it from star-nodes in the Umbra, even...stops making sense. Why do they need that much of the thing?. Mass production of Artifacts it's a good reason to fuel such a hunger as they show in the Lore, so Mage players just assume it. And, even then, PU RAW adds so much juice to the equation that you need to reinterpret it's rules, playing with the word &quot;Value&quot; as meaning something less common than an economist would think, to justify the Technocracy ever needing the juice from other sources. Point being, whatever the amount you think they would need, they prob. have it, or could be interpreted as having it.<br /> <br /> 3\u00b0 You don't need a mage to opperate these Installations that make Devices, Devices that make Devices can be used by normal people. Heck, they can opperate themselves, even. You only need a Mage when the Device it's &quot;original&quot; (that is, when there's not such an installation). Prob. Mages are employed anyway to make sure everything runs smoothly, though. But, again, Mage Industry doesn't need such <i>artesanal</i> quality by pure RAW.<br /> <br /> <i>What stops Technocracy from, one good week, making say 10 factories</i> <i>that make one Talisman every week or so, that allows to turn any propperly equipped place into a factory that ALSO makes Talisman factories that make factories , all of which it's manned by Conditioned normal people - or even none, because Devices can activate themselves - allowing one to increase output exponentially as much as needed prior to the final release. Dare I say, like vampires...</i>But, wait, that it's insane, it would break the setting - Wonders, actual Wonders, aren't supposed to be so common even for the Techocracy...<br /> <br /> Well, on one hand one could say grab the friendly lore and think that Industrialization it's precisely this and just old 'dox ruins mage's life forcing them to crawl when they could soar. But there are other reasons: As said, it costs Quint, and I think that, ultimately, one should go to the point above and say that they have <i>just </i>enough Quintessence to have a lot of production, but not enough to make their artifacts reproduce like vampires :P . Plus making Zones takes time and maybe, something, something, of such an insane (but RAW friendly!) idea it's against the Foundations.<br /> <br /> Now, regardless of that, for the Technocracy this IS the baseline and has been for centuries. All of these dials need to be adjusted to make sense with the setting, but I think you're wrong at thinking the Basic Rules are what limits Mages in regards to production. It's more a <i>relative interpretation </i>about the rules that combines rules and Lore, and goes somewhat beyond the bassic to make a setting that makes some degree of sense. Usually, the main piece of this it's Paradox - coupled with the general conceits about aggregated action and what *should* happen. Also, limiting their undefined - but potentially massive -sources of Quint to a manageable set of assumptions...but this is artificial: Not all Mage STs think the limits work like that, especially in the Umbra and older times, I've seen the floating idea about such von-newman techno-nigthmares. And I don't think it's so much that these didn't got &quot;Mage's RAW about Stuff&quot;, as that such interpretation it's problematic for the Mage setting itself...before adding vampres, and how insignificant they may seem, ever enters into the equation.<br /> <br /> And that's how we get into your interpretation of the situation. That, I think, It's a good one. Just it's wrong in trying to force splats into having &quot;more dakka&quot; because they &quot;RAW can&quot; w/o analizing why they *don't* or *didn't* - Say, why they don't dedicate more people as Fetish builders, if the spirits don't have any problem and they have the resources?, why they didn't built the means of delivery needed to take advantage of it when they have not one, but three Lores relating to movement - or moon bridges. Sometimes, it may even make sense.<br /> <br /> Like the Garou Nation having their own diplomatic take about how much they can entertain Spirits into objects at a given time. As you say, dedicated Fetish builders are rare, that's why Fetishes are rare. But, let's contemplate the possibility that they aren't rare because Garou are primitive and stupid: Maybe if you start to generate Fetishes at Technocratic scale, spirits would regard the Nation as The Scar 2.0<br /> Even Talens are so &quot;cheap&quot;, because the spirits assume they're going to &quot;be released&quot; in one use, I wonder how much you can stash them before they start getting angsty. How many can you stash before someone starts asking for their subordinates. Since they're SOOOOOOOOOOO easy to make, maybe you don't need to have many duplicates, with having enough for one job - then make more - it's enough?<br /> Maybe dedicated Fetish builders aren't that common because there are enough Garou cappable of this to supply the &quot;acceptable demand&quot; (acceptable by the standards of the spirits), and they &quot;dedicate&quot; to build things well, and respectfully, instead of in big numbers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2022, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T17:04:20-07:00","id":1484664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484604#post1484604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there you have it, no wolves in south america at all. Thou werewolves and werefoxes are welcomed to try some weird kinky shit with those guys...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Foxes&quot; cover even animals from reasonably distinct clades, so they're more similar to some foxes than some other foxes, because that's how vulgar names work.<br /> <br /> But take a look later at the thread about the Ratkin species, where we ended up discussing the Garou at length. Given that they could take on Thylacines in Australia, the Manned Wolf is a piece of cake in comparison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484639#post1484639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree in that they're cappable, I'm just saying that they just don't seem to do it. They have their reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but with caveats. And keeping in mind that my original response was to the notion that Mages are undoubtedly more prolific, period, instead of making it a possible interpretation. I was not the first one to consider Talens here, so indeed I'll accept for such purposes any permanently enhanced item (although the whole <i><b>Lore of the Forge</b></i> description was more for completeness sake). I'll consider a whole <i>Voil\u00eb</i> as one such Wonder-like, because it is possible for even the standard one to have extraordinary properties a Changeling can use with ease, although I accept that for all intents and purposes, if a Chimerical Item is exclusively limited to the properties of a mundane version, then it is mundane for our purposes. My main reason to include Chimera here, though, is that it is governed by the same trait as every other enchanted item, a 1-5 dots Background.<br /> <br /> So, first of all, I'll state the reason why I won't work with a Von-Newman set-up: none is given in the setting as anything resembling standard source of special items. As far as we can tell, while possible it is factually not done (taking aside that some such factories <i>may</i> exist as a plot-hook, but they're either not contributing to the Union as a whole, are a ticking bomb almost out of time, or are now out of commission for any reason, they're plot devices, not setting features). For ease of discussion lets call the items just <i>Dakka</i>, despite in this thread it being originally used to refer to old fashioned ammo.<br /> <br /> My observation of the setting is that the Union has a stable output, for sure, but A) most Constructs seem to rely extensively on locally sourced or leased equipment, in opposition to bought Equipment, B) most Union labs and production systems we see are able to produce in a steady pace, but not in an accelerated one, they don't churn hundreds of pieces per day, or even get something finalized every day, C) this production requires direct management by several Mages, as completely autonomous Device Creation Devices are not a standard, either accounting for only a few specific items or just a part of the production process, or even because Enlightened operators can adjust production, D) they put their Equipment at risk of destruction regularly, E) The production is rendered constant by this process, and a huge output would make it overwhelming in no time, F) Horizon Constructs seem to usually demand most of their production because of the nature of Horizon threats, so even without the Avatar Storm they don't count for most of the Equipment on Earth and G) the rules on leasing of Equipment assert several times that those resources are sufficiently scarce to make devolution a big deal if you're not using them.<br /> <br /> None of those indications change that they have a steady, reasonable production that is effective enough to put Dakka on the hands of every Enlightened Agent and a number of Extraordinary Citizens, and we can easily say they're thhe Gold Standard of Dakka production. They're also absolute top dogs in resource management, but that still means that their actual ability to employ Dakka means less production and more effective allocation, that no one can compete with whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Werewolves consider themselves the most important resource in their war, so while a Mage dedicated to production is a perfectly valid member of their group, a Werewolf isn't expected to do this until they grow old and weak. They also need spirits as raw materials, so that puts several limitations you already covered. On the other side, they have an easy and quick process, that is incredibly cheap if they plan for it, and they care with their Dakka means that most permanent items will last for a very long time, which also means they have a lot of accumulated Dakka in stock. Finally they have more numbers, so if both groups have similar &quot;Dakka Per Member Density&quot; (DPMD), then the Garou have more absolute numbers. Add to this that Caerns have Arsenals they lend temporarily to Sept members in mission. I'd say at the end of the day they likely have more total Dakka in their hands on Earth than the Union, while the total output will depend too much on the ST. They do have too much unused items, though, as safety and less reliable inter-Sept logistics means that many Dakka, maybe even the vast majority, are stored at any given time.<br /> <br /> For Demons I'll set aside lost storage as we do not have enough information to know how many relics from the War are left and they only started to procure such Dakka recently. Given the possible proportions of the war, recovering lost arsenals may either make little difference or outright put the Fallen ahead of everyone else. This also means that we can only look at their current capacity for output, not so much accumulated stock. In their current situation, or best, their situation in the early 2000's, I completely agree that they're unlikely to outperform the Union except in personal output, that is, it is completely possible that a single Fallen Artisan can put forward more Dakka than any single Union member with every tool they have to increase their relative output. It won't be so reliable (although it can still be quite reliable), much less so steady, but it is perfectly doable. Their developments since then will make a huge difference, though, so there's little we can say for certain.<br /> <br /> Changelings produce a Voil\u00eb just by undergoing the Crysalis, plus everyone on Earth that is capable of imagination, even really Banal people, produces a Chimera once in a while that a Changeling can use or simply materialize by Invoking the Wyrd. What mainly puts Changelings up front is the ease with which Dakka simply <i>happens</i> around them and they can use it. Most aren't really Dakka as they just do what a mundane counterpart does, but a significant number outperform mundane tools in fantastic ways. They can either get those things in the Dreaming or in the Autumn World. Moments of raw emotion and great significance also increase this natural output of Chimera. Finally, while others are always using very scarce resources to craft Dakka, Changeling artisans can do so with things that are readily available for them. Freeholds are arguably more numerous than any other Standard Place of Power in the WoD and are filled to the brim with Chimera, Chimerical items spontaneously appear here and there, everything they do with dream-stuff becomes a Chimerical Item, and Treasures aren't incredibly distant of the same situation, anyone can make one in a matter of hours out of any trinket bought in an antiquary if they don't want to make it from scratch with more uncommon Dream-Stuff, and hoards of them exist in the Dreaming (maybe spontaneously created, even). It is this tendency for Dream-Dakka to appear out of nowhere and the basic fact that Changelings basically live surrounded by those items that make me believe they're the actual winners in terms of sheer output, while not by merit of their artisans alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T20:20:39-07:00","id":1484667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484664#post1484664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Foxes&amp;quot; cover even animals from reasonably distinct clades, so they're more similar to some foxes than some other foxes, because that's how vulgar names work.<br /> <br /> But take a look later at the thread about the Ratkin species, where we ended up discussing the Garou at length. Given that they could take on Thylacines in Australia, the Manned Wolf is a piece of cake in comparison.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The closest animal to them is a weird carnivor (but still canide) that looks more like mustelide than to anything canide at all, so I'd say they're very far away from any other members of the family.<br /> <br /> They DO ressemble a fox do, but a mix of fox and wolf, but they are bigger than any other wolf while being skinny like a fox... It's very weird, and very unique. It absolutely astonished me when I saw it, it's unlike anything I've ever seen. I dont know if it could be &quot;used&quot; lets call it, by neither Garou or Kitsune","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T23:49:12-07:00","id":1484675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484667#post1484667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest animal to them is a weird carnivor (but still canide) that looks more like mustelide than to anything canide at all, so I'd say they're very far away from any other members of the family.<br /> <br /> They DO ressemble a fox do, but a mix of fox and wolf, but they are bigger than any other wolf while being skinny like a fox... It's very weird, and very unique. It absolutely astonished me when I saw it, it's unlike anything I've ever seen. I dont know if it could be &quot;used&quot; lets call it, by neither Garou or Kitsune</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Garou could breed with the Thylacine, which is a true <u>marsupial</u> who only resembles a wolf due to convergent evolution, and even then not that much, but is ultimately more distant from wolves than any Placentalia mammal. So biologically they're only short of mating with a Platypus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T01:29:35-07:00","id":1484680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484675#post1484675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the Garou could breed with the Thylacine, which is a true <u>marsupial</u> who only resembles a wolf due to convergent evolution, and even then not that much, but is ultimately more distant from wolves than any Placentalia mammal. So biologically they're only short of mating with a Platypus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy, just blame the Mokol\u00e9!<br /> Those lizards are love to mess with genetics; they made a rite just to mate with the mamalians after their race want extinct, but before that, tinekred a bit with their evolution to evolve humanity.... not to mention the Kucha Ekundu, some Tallons made a pact with the mokol\u00e9 to help them breed with the native African wild dogs and the Lycaon pictus is not really in the Cannis genus... basically made a whole new Changer-race<br /> When such things on the table, reality and logic sobs in the corner in WoD and basically mating with a Platypus is possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T03:02:24-07:00","id":1484684,"title":"","content":"It never really made sense to me that the Mokole of Australia would help make breeding with thylacines possible (though also completely unnecessary as dingoes have been on Australia for more than long enough to be the local Garou breeding population, also however the singing dogs of New Guinea can be mated with but dingoes can't), the Mokole of Africa would help the Garou mate with African wild dogs, but the Mokole of South America wouldn't do the same for the maned wolf.<br /> <br /> But, as I've lamented many times in the past, WtA is wildly inconsistent about these things as some of the changers can only breed with a singe species, and others have hundreds if not thousands of potential animals to pick from.<br /> <br /> Though... what does this have to do with vampires again?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T06:40:16-07:00","id":1484697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484675#post1484675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the Garou could breed with the Thylacine, which is a true <u>marsupial</u> who only resembles a wolf due to convergent evolution, and even then not that much, but is ultimately more distant from wolves than any Placentalia mammal. So biologically they're only short of mating with a Platypus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a... Disturbing information... I never really delved THIS DEEP into the reproductive habits of the were-guys and... blergh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T06:44:41-07:00","id":1484698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484684#post1484684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never really made sense to me that the Mokole of Australia would help make breeding with thylacines possible (though also completely unnecessary as dingoes have been on Australia for more than long enough to be the local Garou breeding population, also however the singing dogs of New Guinea can be mated with but dingoes can't), the Mokole of Africa would help the Garou mate with African wild dogs, but the Mokole of South America wouldn't do the same for the maned wolf.<br /> <br /> But, as I've lamented many times in the past, WtA is wildly inconsistent about these things as some of the changers can only breed with a singe species, and others have hundreds if not thousands of potential animals to pick from.<br /> <br /> Though... what does this have to do with vampires again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I always thought the &quot;breeding stock&quot; in Australia would be the dingoes - which is already weird enough. <br /> <br /> Breeding with wolves and humans by itself is... Something already...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T06:49:23-07:00","id":1484699,"title":"","content":"In another topic thou, werewolves ARE part of the folklore in Brazil. My grandfather, who lived in the woods most of his childhood and adolescence, always said that the people in the village had once - not SAW one, no no no... They had CAPTURED a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Real life story that one - not a living captured werewolf (I guess), but someone that believed in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T06:59:48-07:00","id":1484700,"title":"","content":"My friend lives there and he told the tale of &quot;Besta-fera&quot;, The bestial beast, short-tempered and vicious centaur, armed with a flaming whip, who is said to run through villages, followed by a pack of dogs and the sound of its hooves are so frighting, people drop dead of its sound...<br /> I never understood what a centaur is doing in the Amazon, in Brazil...<br /> But used it in a chornicle non the less","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T13:02:04-07:00","id":1484721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484697#post1484697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a... Disturbing information... I never really delved THIS DEEP into the reproductive habits of the were-guys and... blergh!</div> </div> </div> </div>They got help from the Mokole. When you've been through a few mass extinction events, you know how to survive things like the death of your original kin. The only catch is that the new form has to be similar to what it's replacing (that's why Mokole stuck to various reptiles, though they should technically have some bird bloodlines aside from corvids since fuck Linnaeus), but in the case of Homid form, there was apparently a lot of leeway, since the tool-using reptile people that had originally been the analog of this form left no descendants (being entirely fictional) and are only similar to humans in terms of niche and cultural aptitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T18:53:31-07:00","id":1484740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484700#post1484700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friend lives there and he told the tale of &quot;Besta-fera&quot;, The bestial beast, short-tempered and vicious centaur, armed with a flaming whip, who is said to run through villages, followed by a pack of dogs and the sound of its hooves are so frighting, people drop dead of its sound...<br /> I never understood what a centaur is doing in the Amazon, in Brazil...<br /> But used it in a chornicle non the less</div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard of this one, ever, but there's a number of regional legends all across the country. It is, after all, bigger than the contiguous US (The US only surpass Brazil in area due to Alaska).<br /> <br /> But on your main difficulty to understand: contrary to the popular definition of Western Culture in the US, presented in <i>Clash of Civilizations</i> by Samuel P. Huntington, South America in general is actually even more &quot;Western&quot; than the US. The &quot;Latin&quot; in the name is the Roman one, after all. We were also colonized by Europeans and have a lot of the baggage still.<br /> <br /> As a result, many of our folklore is either European in origin or told from the perspective of Europeans dealing with entities from native legends, like the Saci dealing mainly with horses in farms and the Curupira playing deadly pranks on the Bandeirantes. The exceedingly popular tale of the Mula-Sem-Cabe\u00e7a is already pretty centaur-like, although it is actually a headless fire-breathing weremule. So a centaur does not exactly seems so strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484721#post1484721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only catch is that the new form has to be similar to what it's replacing (that's why Mokole stuck to various reptiles, though they should technically have some bird bloodlines aside from corvids since fuck Linnaeus),</div> </div> </div> </div>It's currently a running joke in my games that some Corax call the Mokol\u00e9 posers, as they're the <i>real</i> dinosaurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T19:13:17-07:00","id":1484742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484740#post1484740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's currently a running joke in my games that some Corax call the Mokol\u00e9 posers, as they're the <i>real</i> dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's one of those funny things that the age of the dinosaurs wasn't a continuation of the age of reptiles. It was the reptiles being supplanted by a bunch of mostly flightless birds. The age when the biggest predator was essentially a seven ton chicken.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T21:51:26-07:00","id":1484754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484740#post1484740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's currently a running joke in my games that some Corax call the Mokol\u00e9 posers, as they're the <i>real</i> dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, Mokole aren't trying to be dinosaurs alone, but non-Linnaean Reptilia, and Corax don't include non-avian dinosaurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T22:06:59-07:00","id":1484756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484754#post1484754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, Mokole aren't trying to be dinosaurs alone, but non-Linnaean Reptilia, and Corax don't include non-avian dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. It is a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T07:29:49-07:00","id":1484769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484700#post1484700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friend lives there and he told the tale of &quot;Besta-fera&quot;, The bestial beast, short-tempered and vicious centaur, armed with a flaming whip, who is said to run through villages, followed by a pack of dogs and the sound of its hooves are so frighting, people drop dead of its sound...<br /> I never understood what a centaur is doing in the Amazon, in Brazil...<br /> But used it in a chornicle non the less</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was about to say &quot;Centaur&quot;? What the freaking?<br /> <br /> But then I read &quot;...sound of its hooves are so frighting, people drop dead of its sound...&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh ok, I know what you're talking about. It's not a &quot;Centaur&quot;, maybe your friend failed to properly communicate. It's the &quot;Mula sem Cabe\u00e7a&quot;, or &quot;Headless Mule&quot;, which is exactly that, a Headless Mule. That beast however has a mass of fire in place of it's head. My grandpa also claimed to having witnessing one of those. They are terrifying irrational beasts that destroy everything in their path; if there's one close by, you have to close your eyes and hide your nails so it cant find you. This is one of the most famous monsters of our folklore. It comes from the indigenous natives.<br /> <br /> We also have the &quot;Cuca&quot; (Khukha I guess would be the sound in english) which is a humanoid lizard evil witch; this one fits with Mokoles like a glove, being like a &quot;Crinos&quot; aligator - with magical powers, nonetheless.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Curupira&quot; is a native man with fire hairs and with his feet backwards<br /> <br /> The Ypupiara is a mermaid like sea monsters, but more monstruous than comon mermaids.<br /> <br /> &quot;Saci-Perer\u00ea&quot; is a black man with a single leg who is a trickster with magical powers.<br /> <br /> And perhaps the most famous of all, the &quot;Boto cor de Rosa&quot;, or &quot;Pink Boto&quot;. Boto is the only sweet water dolphin in the world, that lives in the massive amazonic rivers. The natives believe that this animal transforms into a man that impregnates the women of the villages.<br /> <br /> Those are some of the most common myths of brazilian folklore.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, and were beasts too.<br /> <br /> We dont have vampires thou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-23-2022, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T07:43:56-07:00","id":1484771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484769#post1484769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also have the &quot;Cuca&quot; (Khukha I guess would be the sound in english) which is a humanoid lizard evil witch; this one fits with Mokoles like a glove, being like a &quot;Crinos&quot; aligator - with magical powers, nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>It bears saying, the Cuca isn't a native legend, it is Portuguese in origin. Many of the others are also better known by Portuguese retelling than by the original indigenous versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:00:50-07:00","id":1484772,"title":"","content":"And there's also the &quot;Boi-ta-ta&quot;, which is a massive monstruous serpeant that breaths fire.<br /> <br /> I heard about all those long time ago, but I dont remember exactly all the details... There was a tail about the Boi Ta Ta for example that I read as a children of an obstinated farmer that had the fastest horse in the world which was his pride and joy, and became obscessed with hunting the monstruous Boi Ta Ta, but he could never reach it, despite his fast horse, until he became so sick with it that he made his beloved horse give it all it had, finally reaching the monstruous serpent - but his horse ends up dying of exaustion.<br /> <br /> It was something like that, I dont remember what happens after that, it was a kind of Moby Dick like of a story, I dont remember exactly the details, I just remember that at the time I loved it. Brazilian folklore is very weird even for me, and it's also very rich.<br /> <br /> I guess the reason for the weirdness is because it has less &quot;modern contamination&quot; to it - for example, the original greek myths are most of the times vastly different from what our modern pop culture portrays them. Medusa for example, I was shocked to find that it was a CENTAUR like creature, and that her snake-like lower body is a Hollywood invention<br /> <br /> Japanese myth likewise is SUPER weird.<br /> <br /> Even original vampires and werewolves have tons of different tales and myths about, one more strange than the other. The reason why those are a bit more &quot;conventional&quot; is because of extensive modern &quot;padronization&quot; for those, which also includes a ton of rationalization - so for instance, the vampires of Anne Rice have endured an extensive &quot;humanization&quot;, thus they are intelligent humans with supernatural features, instead of simply irrational (and sometimes even with random behavior) undeads.<br /> <br /> So, modern vampires are more appealing to us as modern audiences because we can rationalize their actions, instead of many of the ancient myths that were completely irrational, not following any discernable pattern that could be understandable. For example, in Japan, if you let any object unatended for too long, it could become alive and act in unpredictable ways. That's absolutely terrifying, because it's something completely out of our control.<br /> <br /> Modern views of myths however, rationalize all of their behaviors. Which is why Hollywood werewolves and vampires arent as strange as brazilian or japanese or other myths or others, because they have all been rationalized in their behaviors - werewolves have an infectious curse that turns them into mindless beasts during the full moon, vampires are undead also with an infectious curse that drink blood and burn in the sun. No longer those are the result of arcane curses laid upon by weird sets of occurances that may be outside of people's control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:06:37-07:00","id":1484773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484754#post1484754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, Mokole aren't trying to be dinosaurs alone, but non-Linnaean Reptilia, and Corax don't include non-avian dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Mokole also include turtles in their zoofiliac tendencies?<br /> <br /> &quot;Turtle Ninjas&quot; is suddenly gaining a new weird meaning...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T08:08:24-07:00","id":1484774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484771#post1484771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bears saying, the Cuca isn't a native legend, it is Portuguese in origin. Many of the others are also better known by Portuguese retelling than by the original indigenous versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that, interesting to know. It makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:55:20-07:00","id":1484804,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's not describe anyone's mythologies as super-weird. After all, mythologies are by nature SUPER natural.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T14:15:50-07:00","id":1484807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484773#post1484773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do Mokole also include turtles in their zoofiliac tendencies?<br /> <br /> &quot;Turtle Ninjas&quot; is suddenly gaining a new weird meaning...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what it is, and no, they're dead or gone. The dragons of Ryugu shack up with Same-Bito (Rokea) instead; there is, in fact, a merit for Mokole to be kin to the Same-Bito, indicating a long history of cross-breed relationships. It's one way to stymie the potential birth of The Innocents, I suppose, though W5 is likely making that a thing of the past. I wonder if development is going to filter in more of God-Emperor of Dune to make the Mokole feel more alien by default...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T15:57:10-07:00","id":1484811,"title":"","content":"For other slats in the know, the ultimate deterrent against warring with vampires is the Obfuscate 5 power, Cloak the Gathering. Your dawn-patrol is going to wipe out a lot of neonates, but the coterie or two you didn't find spells silent death or worse. Even those unfamiliar with vampire disciplines would probably hear of stories of groups of vampires who previous hunts failed to account for carrying out retaliatory attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:16:01-07:00","id":1484815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484811#post1484811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For other slats in the know, the ultimate deterrent against warring with vampires is the Obfuscate 5 power, Cloak the Gathering. Your dawn-patrol is going to wipe out a lot of neonates, but the coterie or two you didn't find spells silent death or worse. Even those unfamiliar with vampire disciplines would probably hear of stories of groups of vampires who previous hunts failed to account for carrying out retaliatory attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The &quot;ultimate deterrent against warring vampires&quot; is the fact that, while young vampires are usually piece of shit, in terms of power, the ones who really pull the strings are more often than not beyond the power of most creatures in the world. So, while all the talk about &quot;fighing the elders&quot; young vampires have, it's basically only because of the most ancients vampires that they have any real chance of &quot;unliving&quot;, or better, existing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T17:41:56-07:00","id":1484828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484815#post1484815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;ultimate deterrent against warring vampires&quot; is the fact that, while young vampires are usually piece of shit, in terms of power, the ones who really pull the strings are more often than not beyond the power of most creatures in the world. So, while all the talk about &quot;fighing the elders&quot; young vampires have, it's basically only because of the most ancients vampires that they have any real chance of &quot;unliving&quot;, or better, existing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. There's a lot of things even a starting character in Vampire can do that can give problems to other splats. And there are countermeasures for anything, for and against vampires, although you shouldn't expect any particular splat member to have any particular countermeasure.<br /> <br /> Also, elders &quot;beyond the power of most creatures in the world&quot; aren't at all that common. Most elders are extremely dangerous, but hardly beyond hope to deal with. If an All-Out war were to break out, they wouldn't be any deterrent just with Elder Powers.<br /> <br /> There's no such a thing as a &quot;True Deterrent&quot; except the sheer cost of trying it out. Everyone has means to move about undetected. Everyone has means to notice invisible opponents. Everyone deals with the weird and with a variety of extremely dangerous, versatile and intelligent threats. Everyone would be dead already if they didn't knew how to deal with the others in some capacity.<br /> <br /> Everyone would pay dearly if they tried to just wipe out someone else and even if victorious would be rendered vulnerable to actual threats. That's the real deterrent as far as there is one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T19:32:09-07:00","id":1484833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, elders &quot;beyond the power of most creatures in the world&quot; aren't at all that common. Most elders are extremely dangerous, but hardly beyond hope to deal with. If an All-Out war were to break out, they wouldn't be any deterrent just with Elder Powers. </div> </div> </div>Certainly, most are not &quot;beyond hope to deal with&quot;, in fact, to be honest I think most elders could be easily killed by a starting mage or werewolf character, judging by their character's sheets. What I meant is that one cannot judge the power of an entire splat and the fact that another doesn't just &quot;wipe them out&quot; based on the premise that many (or rather most, in the case of vampires) are weak pieces of shit, there are always ones who are mostly beyond any hope of dealing with, or to put simple, there are probably a few that are beyond your level of power, be you a starting character or even Porthos.<br /> <br /> The same could be said of any splat. I could imagine a similar scenario where one person asks why are werewolves &quot;the punching bag of the WoD&quot; just because you see some allusions here and there of many vampire characters that killed werewolves or even that do it on a regular basis like Talley or Thomas Gerhieren (which is kind of funny because both Thomas and Talley would hardly ever defeat a starting werewolf character alone and mauled in a fight when one judges their rather weak character sheet lol). You can't judge an entire splat just by some poor examples of them, there are many werewolves that are quite beyond the power level of most vampires in the world, and so on, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T08:25:17-07:00","id":1484872,"title":"","content":"The thing is that none of the many &quot;Wars&quot; in WoD are truly unlimited warfare. They are actually &quot;gang raids&quot;, with very restricted local conflicts erupting time to time between local forces.<br /> <br /> That holds true for the Jihad, for Camarilla vs Sabbat assaults, for the &quot;war&quot; between Tremere and Tzimisce or the &quot;Massassa War&quot; of them against the OoH, it's true about the Ascension War or the Weres war against the Wyrm. It's small localized groups maneuvering against one another in the shadows, trying to locate one another, mustering resources when they do and striking at one fortified position at a time when they manage to get a jump on their enemies.<br /> <br /> The only REAL wars in the WoD are waged by Wraiths in the Underworld, between Dark Kingdoms or against countless hordes of Specters during Maelstroms. In those you do indeed can get fights with MILLIONS of forces on each side.<br /> <br /> In any other case, it's a thing of a few dozens of individuals on each side, with a few hundreds on some rare occasions, at most of the time.<br /> <br /> And an &quot;open war&quot; between splats wouldnt be much different, I mean, they all already live constantly into &quot;open wars&quot; amongst themselves - Camarilla vs Sabbat, Traditions vs Technocracy and Weres vs Wyrm. That &quot;open war&quot; however is like a war of attrition between gangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T10:39:22-07:00","id":1484882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484815#post1484815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The &quot;ultimate deterrent against warring vampires&quot; is the fact that, while young vampires are usually piece of shit, in terms of power, the ones who really pull the strings are more often than not beyond the power of most creatures in the world. So, while all the talk about &quot;fighing the elders&quot; young vampires have, it's basically only because of the most ancients vampires that they have any real chance of &quot;unliving&quot;, or better, existing...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure it's not top end power that keeps Werewolves from waring with vampires.<br /> <br /> 1: Vampires can make more vampires very, very quickly. Werewolves reproduce very, very slowly. The disparity is unfathomably severe. Too oversimplify: Assuming you'll get 1 lupus per two batches of wolf cubs, the fastest rate of making werewolves is one every 3-4 years (A lupus will need two years to grow). That's before we get into things like &quot;what if we don't stay honourably mated&quot; or &quot;ecological sustainability&quot; or &quot;the human side of me hates that kind of 'doggy style&quot; or the &quot;Ethics&quot; wyrm fighters are supposed to champion. Vampires on the otherhand need four turns to drain the body, one turn to embrace, and two nights to get the bond bond needed to throw the saps at werewolves. Their concerns are only &quot;How many missing people can I get away with&quot; and &quot;will I get into trouble with other vampires for this&quot;. So long as they've got appropriate weapons, waves upon waves of fledglings will invariably best septs with a little leadership. Garou will ALWAYS lose wars with Vampires. Hows that for an ultimate deterrent?<br /> <br /> 2: Garou need to defend Caerns at all costs. They cannot move Caerns. Caerns are an essential resource for Garou. Vampires essentially just need to defend themselves, with a few like the Ventrue needing to protect their herd or the Tzmisce protecting their jar of dirt. But even then such losses are surmountable. Attacking a Ventrue's herd is a big problem for the Ventrue, but the Ventrue isn't likely to sacrifice himself for it. Werewolves are usually expected to sacrifice themselves for the safety of the Cairn.<br /> <br /> 3: Garou have a few &quot;and fuck the Methuselah&quot; powers. Silent striders specifically have a power that just stops all vampire powers from working. Now, a Methuselah might be able to dart around with 8-dots in physicals and survive a pack who've presumably gotten past other defences with their awesome powers, but it's not likely. (It's worth noting that SS Elders are probably a rarer thing than methuselah)<br /> <br /> :","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T10:58:24-07:00","id":1484884,"title":"","content":"Garou was humilated so many times, that vampires are lucky guys in comparison<br /> <br /> That's why I think ANY Garou (but BSD) deserves to be broken to the level of Theon 'Reek' Greyjoy.<br /> Image... well Albrecht as Reek and... mmm. Vykos as Ramsy.<br /> What a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T11:40:25-07:00","id":1484885,"title":"","content":"Well, given the nerf job that V5 got and the fact that werewolves don't seem to be anywhere near the danger that they were in V20 (In Chicago by night, vampires with ridiculously weak stats are said to be veritable werewolves killers) I think garous are going to be beaten with the nerf stick even harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T12:16:09-07:00","id":1484886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484882#post1484882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure it's not top end power that keeps Werewolves from waring with vampires.<br /> <br /> 1: Vampires can make more vampires very, very quickly. Werewolves reproduce very, very slowly. The disparity is unfathomably severe. Too oversimplify: Assuming you'll get 1 lupus per two batches of wolf cubs, the fastest rate of making werewolves is one every 3-4 years (A lupus will need two years to grow). That's before we get into things like &quot;what if we don't stay honourably mated&quot; or &quot;ecological sustainability&quot; or &quot;the human side of me hates that kind of 'doggy style&quot; or the &quot;Ethics&quot; wyrm fighters are supposed to champion. Vampires on the otherhand need four turns to drain the body, one turn to embrace, and two nights to get the bond bond needed to throw the saps at werewolves. Their concerns are only &quot;How many missing people can I get away with&quot; and &quot;will I get into trouble with other vampires for this&quot;. So long as they've got appropriate weapons, waves upon waves of fledglings will invariably best septs with a little leadership. Garou will ALWAYS lose wars with Vampires. Hows that for an ultimate deterrent?<br /> <br /> 2: Garou need to defend Caerns at all costs. They cannot move Caerns. Caerns are an essential resource for Garou. Vampires essentially just need to defend themselves, with a few like the Ventrue needing to protect their herd or the Tzmisce protecting their jar of dirt. But even then such losses are surmountable. Attacking a Ventrue's herd is a big problem for the Ventrue, but the Ventrue isn't likely to sacrifice himself for it. Werewolves are usually expected to sacrifice themselves for the safety of the Cairn.<br /> <br /> 3: Garou have a few &quot;and fuck the Methuselah&quot; powers. Silent striders specifically have a power that just stops all vampire powers from working. Now, a Methuselah might be able to dart around with 8-dots in physicals and survive a pack who've presumably gotten past other defences with their awesome powers, but it's not likely. (It's worth noting that SS Elders are probably a rarer thing than methuselah)<br /> <br /> :</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires sleep all day and Garou are uniquely designed to be able to find them and slaughter an army of them with ease. The risk involved in creating a lot of shovelheads is not a small thing. It can easily result in the entire crop of shovelheads and their creators being destroyed by mundane hunters before the garou even get involved. And the result is a bunch of people with no skills, maybe one or two dots of disciplines, who easily panic when facing monsters the size of the Hulk. And garou have allies themselves: spirits, some of whom can manifest in the real world and are effectively immortal. I've been running and playing in games where creating shovelheads is a routine thing for decades. They are a far more minor and situational tool than you seem to think they are.<br /> <br /> Here's the reality: werewolves can easily find you no matter how well hidden you think you are. Werewolves can kill you easily at night, and effortlessly during the day. And there is nothing you can do to stop them, because they have multiple ways of either neutralizing any static defenses, or teleporting around them. Even weapons don't matter, because they have the power to simply shut weapons off. I feel silly even calling them &quot;werewolves&quot;. Werewolves don't have massive superspeed and lightsaber fingernails or interdimensional teleportation. What they are is Quicksilver with a lightsaber and a Rick Sanchez portal gun and a bunch of I-WIN buttons to easily counter anything you construct or prepare to stop them. There is no war between garou and vampires; there is only pest control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-24-2022, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T16:48:33-07:00","id":1484907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484833#post1484833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certainly, most are not &amp;quot;beyond hope to deal with&amp;quot;, in fact, to be honest I think most elders could be easily killed by a starting mage or werewolf character, judging by their character's sheets. What I meant is that one cannot judge the power of an entire splat and the fact that another doesn't just &amp;quot;wipe them out&amp;quot; based on the premise that many (or rather most, in the case of vampires) are weak pieces of shit, there are always ones who are mostly beyond any hope of dealing with, or to put simple, there are probably a few that are beyond your level of power, be you a starting character or even Porthos.<br /> <br /> The same could be said of any splat. I could imagine a similar scenario where one person asks why are werewolves &amp;quot;the punching bag of the WoD&amp;quot; just because you see some allusions here and there of many vampire characters that killed werewolves or even that do it on a regular basis like Talley or Thomas Gerhieren (which is kind of funny because both Thomas and Talley would hardly ever defeat a starting werewolf character alone and mauled in a fight when one judges their rather weak character sheet lol). You can't judge an entire splat just by some poor examples of them, there are many werewolves that are quite beyond the power level of most vampires in the world, and so on, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire Methusas are beyond ridiculous. They are the most powerful individuals of the entire splats, and no Were or Mage or Fairy can compare.<br /> <br /> To begin with, it doesnt matter how smart or brilliant of a tactician a Garou or a Mage can be; a 4th gen vamp can get up to Intelligence 9. With that ridiculous stat you dont even need disciplines or any other sort of supernatural &quot;mojo&quot; - at least if we were to be realistic here, game mechanics more often than not will screw over realism but that's another story.<br /> <br /> Intellugence 5 is super genius; intelligence 9 is unfatomable for our human imagination. Such a being would basically be able to predict any outcome, to surpass any plot and to prepare plans you couldnt even conceive, without ever having to summon his vodoo at all. There's a reason why the younger vampires think they are pawns into the elders games - it's because it's true. Those elders set plans in motion and they play a game of chess that plan for centuries of moves ahead of time.<br /> <br /> Then you go to other traits, like Perception 8-9, Wits 8-9. Do you have any idea what would that mean? 8 or 9 Perception? That's like hearing the sound of leafs falling, or seeing a small bug walking over a leaf while you're flying in a helicopter over a jungle. And wits 9 would be like solving all Quantum Mechanics equations while you calculate the distances of all visible stars with your naked eye all in your head in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> Then we go to the social traits. What the hell even means to have 9 of beauty? That would be transcedental, you would probably cause allucinations on mortals, or cause an hypnotic stance. Appearence 9 is something divine-like, some angelic stuff that probably would cause even other supernaturals to go insane! Or make them obscessed into trying to gain your favor. That's something completely beyond our imagination.<br /> <br /> Manipulation 8-9 and Charisma 8-9 means that all those Methusas have to do is to open their mouths and you'll immediatly fall in love with them. With Charisma 8-9 you'll love the guy more than your own mother, and with Manipulation 8-9 means he could convince you that killing your own mother would be for the benefit of both you and your mother.<br /> <br /> Then comes all the skills, with the same ridiculous capabilities for level 8-9. And the same considerations as for attributes go - and I wont ever cover physical attributes because there's no need to.<br /> <br /> Just imagine Dexterity 8 Stealth 8. You effectively dont even need Obfuscate with that! Or Manipulation 8 Subterfuge 8? It's as if you had Dominate!<br /> <br /> And finally we go to the disciplines, and now things get really insane. Auspex 8-9? Obfuscate 8-9? Fortitude 8-9? Domination and Presence 8-9? Celerity 8-9? <br /> <br /> And that's just to keep with the common ones, because going with the exclusively ones - like Quietus, Quimeirism, Thaumaturgy etc etc it's all several levels of absurd.<br /> <br /> And Im not even considering the ones that go to lvl 10!<br /> <br /> Even 7th or 6th gens who get traits at 6 or 7 are amazingly impressive and more than a challenge for any splat.<br /> <br /> Besides all that, those eldars are cunning as hell. You simply do NOT find them - period. They find YOU.<br /> <br /> Yes, those are responsible for a good amount of the capabilities of the splat, but the real reason neonates arent constantly exterminated by angry weres and power hungry mages is because all splats are busy with their own problems and cant add to that going out of their ways just to open up a new front in their many endless attrition gang wars to do that and further weaken their positions by going after other splats that simply arent bothering them.<br /> <br /> In fact, one of the smarter groups in that aspect is the Technocracy; their main focus are the Mages, obviously, but they will hunt down any splat stupid enough to try to come into the open.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats however dont bother themselves all too much with vampires, particularly the Camarilla. In fact, both groups operate as if they had a sort of silent unofficial agreement, or rather they follow mutual purposes and agendas that are mutually beneficial. The Technocracy wants to erradicate the supernatural, and the Camarilla wants to keep it hidden; both groups end up aiding one another even if unwillingly and unkowingly, and they stay of each other's harms ways. Why would the Technocracy devote precious resources hunting vamps that keep to themselves and even hunt nasty stuff for you?<br /> <br /> In fact, the Tecnocracy hates Werebeasts and Changellings far more than they hate vampires.<br /> <br /> So this is way the neonates are relatively safe as long as they arent stupid from the other splats.<br /> <br /> Elders are still important, but far more so to protect the neonates against other vampires than against other splats that simply have no interest in them.<br /> <br /> And the same can be said to any splat - an Archmaster aint what keep the vampires and weres at bay - those keep themselves at bay by not caring about Mages, but the Archmasters keep the Technocrats away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T06:14:51-07:00","id":1484960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484907#post1484907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire Methusas are beyond ridiculous. They are the most powerful individuals of the entire s