"custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T06:46:10-07:00","id":1484962,"title":"","content":"There's enough bullshit at the higher end tiers for all of the splats that it's plausible that any one vs one confrontation could end in the favor of one splat or another. For example, werewolves have a gift that just stops vampires from being able to spend blood points. If a werewolf hits a Methuselah that's invested most of their exp into Disciplines that require blood point expenditures than goes in for the attack, that Methuselah is very likely going to die. On the other hand, if the Methuselah has invested more heavily into Disciplines that don't require blood points, then he's likely not terribly affected and you're going to probably end up with a dead (or Dominated) werewolf.<br /> <br /> Ultimately any sort of confrontation runs into the issue that characters won't have every single Discipline or Gift or Sphere, and so they're going to end up with potential holes that another splat could exploit to defeat them.<br /> <br /> This is also how things are explained &quot;in game&quot; where you might have splats defeating one another in ways that &quot;don't make sense&quot; in terms of optimized white room combat. Going along with this, in the idea of vampire vs werewolf, in general from the in-game perspective, a werewolf will defeat a vampire. A pack of vampires can defeat a werewolf. An Elder vampire can defeat a werewolf, but a pack of werewolves will kill an elder. Then you get into Methuselahs who are capable of killing packs of werewolves. Of course then you have Rank 5 Garou and a pack of those guys will trash most any Methuselahs unless they're on the level of someone like Baba Yaga and even then that sort of fight could go either way.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the most powerful of vampires (Antediluvians) sit on the apex of the WoD power level scale, on par with Wyrm Talons, Yama Kings, Neverborn, etc. Defeating one is something that would take multiple werewolf tribes, or a huge cross section of the Technocracy to oppose and (possibly) defeat.<br /> <br /> So vampires are both the &quot;punching bag&quot; of the WoD and also some of the most powerful and dangerous critters in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T13:38:26-07:00","id":1484983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1484886#post1484886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Werewolves don't have massive superspeed and lightsaber fingernails or interdimensional teleportation. What they are is Quicksilver with a lightsaber and a Rick Sanchez portal gun and a bunch of I-WIN buttons to easily counter anything you construct or prepare to stop them. There is no war between garou and vampires; there is only pest control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horror movie monsters frequently possess off-screen movement that defies what one might consider a proper flow of time, can tear through targets as if they were wet paper, and are exactly where you would most hope they wouldn't be. The Garou pretty much entirely encapsulate this and not what you just described - except perhaps for being as fast as Quicksilver, but that just contributes to the horror, like in Dead Man's Chest when Captain Jack spotted Davy Jones in his spyglass, far off in the distance, and the next moment, Jones is just standing there next to him.<br /> <br /> W:tA employs a lot of splatter. Anyone could die at any time; get involved with this distinct sub-genre of horror at your own risk, introspective personal torture fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T14:28:52-07:00","id":1485208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> still remember how broken temporis, serpentis and obtenebration were in dark ages </div> </div> </div>I struggle to think of any &quot;broken&quot; power from serpentis or even worse, obtenebration. Most obtenebration powers are ridiculously lackluster, seems like people ran out of ideas or something worse, because a level 6 power that sends a shadow to suck a bit of blood from someone is shockingly ridiculously weak, perhaps for a level two power AT MOST it would perhaps be a bit interesting, but a level 6 power!? Also, Ahriman's Demesne, a level 9 power that you need to tell people &quot;wait please, I need 3 turns to cause half the damage a neonate gangrel is going to deal in half a turn&quot;. I struggle to understand how people are paid to develop such lackluster powers and even v20 with all the great things it did, didn't fix many of these ridiculous things...that reminds me of the reason usually give my friends who gave up on playing vampire: &quot;I house rule basically EVERYTHING&quot;. The WoD is great and all, and the reason I love the game is the setting, because I'm most of the time dumbfounded that there are SO MANY poorly designed vampire powers in the game. At least mage solves it elegantly with the great system for power it has, and many gifts were made by people who really wanted to make werewolf shine, in complete disregard to their poorly designed &quot;vampire cousin's&quot; powers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T15:51:44-07:00","id":1485218,"title":"","content":"'it's worth noting that SS Elders are probably a rarer thing than methuselah' I know this is off topic but when you said this my first thought was 'what do nazi vampires have to do with this ' lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T17:18:13-07:00","id":1485234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=