oken&quot; power from serpentis or even worse, obtenebration. Most obtenebration powers are ridiculously lackluster, seems like people ran out of ideas or something worse, because a level 6 power that sends a shadow to suck a bit of blood from someone is shockingly ridiculously weak, perhaps for a level two power AT MOST it would perhaps be a bit interesting, but a level 6 power!? Also, Ahriman's Demesne, a level 9 power that you need to tell people &quot;wait please, I need 3 turns to cause half the damage a neonate gangrel is going to deal in half a turn&quot;. I struggle to understand how people are paid to develop such lackluster powers and even v20 with all the great things it did, didn't fix many of these ridiculous things...that reminds me of the reason usually give my friends who gave up on playing vampire: &quot;I house rule basically EVERYTHING&quot;. The WoD is great and all, and the reason I love the game is the setting, because I'm most of the time dumbfounded that there are SO MANY poorly designed vampire powers in the game. At least mage solves it elegantly with the great system for power it has, and many gifts were made by people who really wanted to make werewolf shine, in complete disregard to their poorly designed &quot;vampire cousin's&quot; powers...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the other side, Temporis is a hell of a &quot;broken&quot; discipline, it accomplishes everything it's supposed to do and even more, even if it's a bit broken (I most of the time ban it, if the game is only about vampires), there is no denying that it's in fact a very well-developed discipline, all of its powers are thematic and good at the same time, no &quot;nonsense&quot; power and much less any useless power (like what happen to Obtenebration, Valeren and countless others), something very rare among vampire disciplines. One could argue that, while some people talk about Thaumaturgy being op, Temporis is the &quot;\u00fcber&quot; discipline, it alone is enough to make a vampire stand against most things that could come on his way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T21:02:46-07:00","id":1485251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485246#post1485246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the other side, Temporis is a hell of a &amp;quot;broken&amp;quot; discipline, it accomplishes everything it's supposed to do and even more, even if it's a bit broken (I most of the time ban it, if the game is only about vampires), there is no denying that it's in fact a very well-developed discipline, all of its powers are thematic and good at the same time, no &amp;quot;nonsense&amp;quot; power and much less any useless power (like what happen to Obtenebration, Valeren and countless others), something very rare among vampire disciplines. One could argue that, while some people talk about Thaumaturgy being op, Temporis is the &amp;quot;\u00fcber&amp;quot; discipline, it alone is enough to make a vampire stand against most things that could come on his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporis is absolutely insane. Much more than Thaumaturgy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T23:23:26-07:00","id":1485264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485246#post1485246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other side, Temporis is a hell of a &quot;broken&quot; discipline, it accomplishes everything it's supposed to do and even more, even if it's a bit broken (I most of the time ban it, if the game is only about vampires), there is no denying that it's in fact a very well-developed discipline, all of its powers are thematic and good at the same time, no &quot;nonsense&quot; power and much less any useless power (like what happen to Obtenebration, Valeren and countless others), something very rare among vampire disciplines. One could argue that, while some people talk about Thaumaturgy being op, Temporis is the &quot;\u00fcber&quot; discipline, it alone is enough to make a vampire stand against most things that could come on his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my reservation about that.<br /> <br /> The problem with <b>Temporis</b> is that level 5 basically makes it. <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> is basically <b>Celerity</b> on steroids, which I think is a really bad design for being already too close to another Discipline on one level alone (and better at it than the original). It is even worse on V20 with <b>Celerity</b> nerfed. The comparison, not the nerf itself, it was absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> Leave this single power out and <b>Temporis</b> is average at most, with the added problem of demanding <b>Auspex</b> for the most useful effects to be accessible. The first level is just too situational, and if properly heightened to become a true Time-related <b><i>Heightened Senses</i></b> it would be more than enough to ditch the need of Auspex for those effects without supplanting actual <b>Auspex</b>.<br /> <br /> So my take from it isn't that <b>Temporis</b> is broken, it is that <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> needs a nerf on par with <b>Celerity</b> or greater, or just be ditched completely in favor of other time-related power (yeah, the story of <b>Celerity</b> being watered down <b>Temporis</b> is funny, but is a bad guide for design and can be achieved with a hypothetical level 7 or 8 power instead). Once that's achieved, add a few improvements to the other powers so they come to be on par with other disciplines and it is ready to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T06:10:21-07:00","id":1485277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which I think is a really bad design for being already too close to another Discipline </div> </div> </div>Well, I think it being similar to another discipline, especially celerity, is really thematic and in the end, almost unavoidable when one thinks of time/speed powers. It happens with basically every splat across the WoD, but in the case of Temporis, because of the relationship between <i>True</i> Brujah and Brujah, it's even feels fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he problem with <b>Temporis</b> is that level 5 basically makes it. <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> </div> </div> </div>While there's no denying that Clotho's Gift is in fact very powerful (it's the power I feel the need to curb or ban), I consider every level of Temporis from 1 to 5 as very useful and good. Only level 2 is already enough to &quot;break&quot; an enemy fighter, or at the very least put up a good resistance, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I think that in the end, what makes Clotho's Gift op is what makes Celerity op, it's the fact that multiple actions utterly breaks the Storyteller system. It's better than anything else and it's the reason why I chose to disallow multiple actions in most of my games (crossovers included), following what seems to be a great idea from Requiem. The problem I face is how to balance such powers, i.e. how do I rework Clotho's Gift to be good on a game where noone is supposed to take multiple actions. This is a problem I'm facing right now, btw, in other words, I'm trying to think of a way to make it work &quot;in a world where multiple actions don't exist&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T07:11:24-07:00","id":1485284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485264#post1485264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my reservation about that.<br /> <br /> The problem with <b>Temporis</b> is that level 5 basically makes it. <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> is basically <b>Celerity</b> on steroids, which I think is a really bad design for being already too close to another Discipline on one level alone (and better at it than the original). It is even worse on V20 with <b>Celerity</b> nerfed. The comparison, not the nerf itself, it was absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> Leave this single power out and <b>Temporis</b> is average at most, with the added problem of demanding <b>Auspex</b> for the most useful effects to be accessible. The first level is just too situational, and if properly heightened to become a true Time-related <b><i>Heightened Senses</i></b> it would be more than enough to ditch the need of Auspex for those effects without supplanting actual <b>Auspex</b>.<br /> <br /> So my take from it isn't that <b>Temporis</b> is broken, it is that <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> needs a nerf on par with <b>Celerity</b> or greater, or just be ditched completely in favor of other time-related power (yeah, the story of <b>Celerity</b> being watered down <b>Temporis</b> is funny, but is a bad guide for design and can be achieved with a hypothetical level 7 or 8 power instead). Once that's achieved, add a few improvements to the other powers so they come to be on par with other disciplines and it is ready to go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are being too hard on temporis, granted I don't remember the exact powers since I played both versions of dark ages but the second and 3rd dot of the discipline are pretty damn useful, hell leaden movement allows you to severely compromise a celerity user if not outright nullify the power and while I agree that Clotho's gift is ridiculosly powerful you have to remember that activating other disciplines (which is the main aspect that Clotho's gift has over celerity) causes 2 unsoakable levels of lethal damage so while you are definitely going to be a powerhouse it is still not so much broken to warrant an heavier nerf than celerity. Regarding the first level, yeah I agree it's pretty fucking useless, it would have been better if they allowed you to wake up at the exact same time as the sun went down so to make it a little more useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T07:21:35-07:00","id":1485286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485277#post1485277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think it being similar to another discipline, especially celerity, is really thematic and in the end, almost unavoidable when one thinks of time/speed powers. It happens with basically every splat across the WoD, but in the case of Temporis, because of the relationship between <i>True</i> Brujah and Brujah, it's even feels fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a design perspective, if you're going to make two traits that are distinct and concurrent, they need to follow three criteria:<br /> <br /> 1 - Be distinct enough that players can appreciate the choice between one and the other as meaningful;<br /> <br /> 2 - Be &quot;balanced&quot; enough that players can see reason to take one or the other depending on circumstances;<br /> <br /> 3 - Be able to pass those tests on most occasions, instead of just in exceedingly strict scenarios.<br /> <br /> The problem with <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> is that it isn't just similar to <b>Celerity</b>, but that it completely substitutes <b>Celerity</b>. While it follows a somewhat distinct mechanic, it is too similar to <b>Celerity</b> in the final effect to be said the difference is meaningful and the only advantage <b>Celerity</b> has is giving bonus Dex in V20, which simply does not beat 3 BP to get several extra action for 3 rounds or more, specially when that will be just one power, not the whole of the Discipline.<br /> <br /> If it was the whole of <b>Temporis</b>, then things would be a tad better. If <b>Celerity</b> still cost 1 BP for complete activation, then it would be better balanced. In both cases there would be meaningful advantages in either choice, but they would be so similar that still any player that found their own preferred mechanic would simply ditch the other Discipline for all characters.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> could have more distinct mechanics still following on the theme of accelerating through time. Or it could be an Elder Level and level 5 be another thematic power. <i><b>Kiss of Lachesis</b></i> could, with just minor adjustments, be a good enough level 5 power, and is my go to simple substitute for <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485277#post1485277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there's no denying that Clotho's Gift is in fact very powerful (it's the power I feel the need to curb or ban), I consider every level of Temporis from 1 to 5 as very useful and good. Only level 2 is already enough to &quot;break&quot; an enemy fighter, or at the very least put up a good resistance, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, just not nearly as much (comparatively).<br /> <br /> Specially when you add their costs, rolls and requirements for effective use, they're a little below average in comparison with most other Disciplines, This is not the worst, it is still close to average and very useful indeed, it <b>is</b> a solid Discipline choice. But I think the majority of those powers could use a little tweak here and there to really be on par with the others, nothing major.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue in this sense is <b><i>Hourglass of the Mind</i></b>. Seriously, a perfect sense of time is neat, but a 1-point Merit at most. And the sense that <i>something</i> happened to time, without the ability to say what, and still with an <i>Awareness</i> roll at normal difficulty, this is another Merit, 2-points at most, probably 1. Even combined it simply does not make it for even a first level power, at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485277#post1485277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in the end, what makes Clotho's Gift op is what makes Celerity op, it's the fact that multiple actions utterly breaks the Storyteller system. It's better than anything else and it's the reason why I chose to disallow multiple actions in most of my games (crossovers included), following what seems to be a great idea from Requiem. The problem I face is how to balance such powers, i.e. how do I rework Clotho's Gift to be good on a game where noone is supposed to take multiple actions. This is a problem I'm facing right now, btw, in other words, I'm trying to think of a way to make it work &quot;in a world where multiple actions don't exist&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple actions do not work in any system whatsoever, not without very clear boundaries to limit its effectiveness.<br /> <br /> You can take a clue from Requiem again, benefits on Movement and Initiative are usually good. Another option is to let the <i>description</i> of an action be of multiple, fast-paced repetitions of the same task, but the <i>mechanical effect</i> be just a bonus to the action, something M&amp;M 2nd ed does. As a wild example, <b>Celerity</b> could just let you spend 1 BP to turn the bonus dice to automatic successes, or to reduce the difficulty of a Dex-based task, including both attack and defense.<br /> <br /> Another option, which may be interesting for <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b>, is to follow the rules in D&amp;D's <b>Time Stop</b>, where the limit is due how long the world takes to react to your actions, so direct interaction becomes tricky, but there are clear uses. This make some sense if you consider that while your movement is &quot;faster&quot;, it still carries the same energy and the transference isn't completely in your new time flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T08:34:16-07:00","id":1485293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the only advantage <b>Celerity</b> has is giving bonus Dex in V20 </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Dex is an \u00fcber attribute in the Storyteller System, to the point I'm thinking about nerfing celerity, making it cost blood to activate, etc. Even though my games don't have multiple actions, the flat bonus to dexterity makes it perhaps too powerful just for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Kiss of Lachesis</b></i> could, with just minor adjustments, be a good enough level 5 power, and is my go to simple substitute for <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b>. </div> </div> </div>My problem with <i>Kiss of Lachesis </i>is that it's a broken power, I mean, with even just 3 successes you send a cainite straight to torpor, so it's basically one &quot;I win button&quot;. Something I HATE in any given power and the reason why I think the gifts <i>Dam the Heartflood</i> and <i>Paws of the newborn cub</i> are terrible designs. I think any such powers should allow a resistance on the other end, if you have a power that is potentially one &quot;I win button&quot;, IMO it MUST allow a resistance test to your opponent, otherwise it's broken. I also don't like the fact that you need to touch, as I don't think it's very thematic and reminds me too much of <i>Hands of Destruction's Turn to Dust</i> that in turn, reminds me of <i>Grave's Decay Dissolve the Flesh</i> (albeit this time, not so close). But the latter is more of a small nuisance, not a big deal, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My biggest issue in this sense is <b><i>Hourglass of the Mind</i></b>. Seriously, a perfect sense of time is neat, but a 1-point Merit at most. And the sense that <i>something</i> happened to time, without the ability to say what, and still with an <i>Awareness</i> roll at normal difficulty, this is another Merit, 2-points at most, probably 1. Even combined it simply does not make it for even a first level power, at all. </div> </div> </div>I agree that it's a weak power, but then again most level 1 powers are like this, even for Mages that are the &quot;\u00fcber splat&quot; of WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a wild example, <b>Celerity</b> could just let you spend 1 BP to turn the bonus dice to automatic successes, or to reduce the difficulty of a Dex-based task, including both attack and defense. </div> </div> </div>I have a problem with that, because if you allow one to spends blood to turn the bonus Dex from Celerity into <i>automatic</i> successes, it would make <i>Flower of Death</i> redundant and it's a freaking level 7 power.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm all ears (or rather, &quot;all eyes&quot;) for any suggestion of how to rework these things for my games. At the moment no player has Temporis in any of my tables, but I need to have a rework at hand for the case it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T14:49:07-07:00","id":1485315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> causes 2 unsoakable levels of lethal damage so while you are definitely going to be a powerhouse it is still not so much broken to warrant an heavier nerf than celerity. </div> </div> </div>True, this is certainly a good deterrent to any abuse of the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other side, Temporis is a hell of a &quot;broken&quot; discipline, it accomplishes everything it's supposed to do and even more </div> </div> </div>Here, I was naturally talking about the DAV20 rework of the discipline. I don't quite like the one in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, there are many &quot;weird&quot; powers there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T19:20:25-07:00","id":1485328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485293#post1485293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, Dex is an \u00fcber attribute in the Storyteller System, to the point I'm thinking about nerfing celerity, making it cost blood to activate, etc. Even though my games don't have multiple actions, the flat bonus to dexterity makes it perhaps too powerful just for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the sentiment, but I don't think it is so relevant. Dex is the all-purpose go-to to see if a physical action <i>happens</i>, but it has little say in how effective many such actions actually are. Strength affects damage, carrying capacity, jump and similar stuff directly and Stamina absorbs damage as many times as damage occurs, so while Dex almost always applies, it almost never is the most significant factor in the actual result. And both Potence and Fortitude add directly to the Attributes.<br /> <br /> As we talk about them before house-ruling when talking about their effectiveness, no Dex bonus can remotely compare to simply being able to perform multiple actions. Also, the problem remains that <b>Celerity</b> in its entirety is being compared to a single <b>Temporis</b> level, so the Dex bonus should be compared to the rest of <b>Temporis</b>, as you have to have the other four levels first anyway. <b>Celerity</b>, as the other Physical Disciplines, has the problem of not adding anything new at each level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485293#post1485293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with <i>Kiss of Lachesis </i>is that it's a broken power</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anymore, in V20 they eliminated the &quot;I Win Button&quot;. Its main use now is on objects and mortals, and even then it takes a lot of successes to accomplish an &quot;I Win&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> Also, that's why I said it needs minor adjustments.<br /> <br /> Look at everything that has a number, directly or not, in a Discipline as a dial. You can change a lot of how it plays just messing with the dials.<br /> <br /> I'd change difficulty and maybe the age table on <i><b>Kiss</b></i>, possibly give it some range. Compare to other level 5 powers to see where it can improve or should be nerfed, but by V20 it is already pretty close to usable at level 5 or lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485293#post1485293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it's a weak power, but then again most level 1 powers are like this, even for Mages that are the &quot;\u00fcber splat&quot; of WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to this degree. I'm re-reading every level 1 Discipline power in the V20 core and can count on the fingers of one hand those that are arguably as generally useless: <b>Dementation</b>, <b>Bone Path</b> and <b>Cenotaph Path</b>. Every single other Discipline/Path has a level 1 power that is useful in a greater range of situations, more useful when they come into play, useful in situations the character can go after, or a combination of those.<br /> <br /> But I don't think <b><i>Hourglass</i></b> have to be fundamentally changed, the concept is perfectly fine, it is the mechanics that can and should be improved. The very least would be to be able to roll something to get more information on Time distortions, plus make perception not only precise in timing events, but also able to do things like noticing every frame of a movie and other split-second perceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485293#post1485293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a problem with that, because if you allow one to spends blood to turn the bonus Dex from Celerity into <i>automatic</i> successes, it would make <i>Flower of Death</i> redundant and it's a freaking level 7 power.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>Flower of Death</i></b> isn't important to begin with. No specific Elder Level power is, they're just examples in the end, so I don't see a big problem there.<br /> <br /> But then you go with the other suggestion, make it reduce Difficulty. For <b>Celerity</b> it could be a 1 to 1 reduction for BP spent, or maybe half of your Celerity rating rounded up, but then you loose the Dex bonus (like it currently happens when you take multiple actions). Another option with automatic successes could be that instead of adding X successes, it adds 1 success for the next X actions.<br /> <br /> Finally there's the option of limiting the extra actions to pure movement or something like that, so the character can't really roll more times, but can cross large distances. That's already almost Requiem's <b>Celerity</b> and you can simply copy-past it, maybe together with the other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T02:07:06-07:00","id":1485345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it has little say in how effective many such actions actually are. </div> </div> </div>Well, the net successes above the opponent's defensive actions already gives a huge say in &quot;how effective many such actions actually are&quot;, but I understand not everyone use this rule for every kind of attack. One very important thing to notice is that celerity is a passive discipline, so it's quite different from Temporis, also the damage one takes to use extra actions is, as mentioned, a strong deterrent to abuse Clotho's Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not anymore, in V20 they eliminated the &quot;I Win Button&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'd say the very opposite, the DAV20 version is even more powerful than before, as it explicitly states that 3 or more successes would send a target cainite straight into torpor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> no Dex bonus can remotely compare to simply being able to perform multiple actions. </div> </div> </div>Certainly you are correct, there's nothing more &quot;broken&quot; than multiple actions in the Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Flower of Death</i></b> isn't important to begin with. No specific Elder Level power is, they're just examples in the end, so I don't see a big problem there </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree here and I think this reasoning is perhaps why we see so many either broken or utterly garbage advanced powers in every splat, they (the writers) may think it's irrelevant, but it's certainly not. It creates precedent, it &quot;exist&quot; and players (and storytellers like me) are going to notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't think <b><i>Hourglass</i></b> have to be fundamentally changed, the concept is perfectly fine, it is the mechanics that can and should be improved. </div> </div> </div>I agree with you here, the power's concept is great and very thematic, perhaps it could see a buff, but not a strong one.<br /> <br /> Regarding Clotho's Gift, I'm thinking that perhaps adding the level of Temporis as extra dices to the action to represent what the &quot;accelerated time&quot; actions could mean is a possibility. What do you think? Another possibility is to go ahead and use <i>KIss of Lachesis</i>, but give the opponent a resist roll, as I make with most &quot;I win button&quot; powers, like <i>Paws of the Newborn Curb</i>, among others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:34:18-07:00","id":1485578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485345#post1485345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the net successes above the opponent's defensive actions already gives a huge say in &quot;how effective many such actions actually are&quot;, but I understand not everyone use this rule for every kind of attack. One very important thing to notice is that celerity is a passive discipline, so it's quite different from Temporis, also the damage one takes to use extra actions is, as mentioned, a strong deterrent to abuse Clotho's Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering the net successes rule, already, otherwise I don't think you would even consider Dex so powerful.<br /> <br /> Even with net successes going to damage, they're not a direct effect of Dex: you need the net successes, first. That's what I meant, while a +1 to Str will be +1 dice to damage, a +1 to Dex will do that only of it is a success on attack, which is less than 50% with dif 7 and the rule of 1.<br /> <br /> For being passive, that's countered by <b>Temporis</b> having other 4 levels of powers, so lets compare +5 Dex to 4 utility powers, including a perception one that's also passive.<br /> <br /> And the damage in <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> is only for Discipline activation, if you use it under the same constrain of <b>Celerity</b> it has no damage. It isn't a better extra actions setup counterbalanced by damage, it is a better extra actions setup <i>before</i> the fact it lets you pay with damage to be even more broken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485345#post1485345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the very opposite, the DAV20 version is even more powerful than before, as it explicitly states that 3 or more successes would send a target cainite straight into torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I didn't referenced DAV20, I said V20. DAV in any edition is a mixed bag as far as powers go, I never take it as default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485345#post1485345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree here and I think this reasoning is perhaps why we see so many either broken or utterly garbage advanced powers in every splat, they (the writers) may think it's irrelevant, but it's certainly not. It creates precedent, it &quot;exist&quot; and players (and storytellers like me) are going to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, we don't disagree in this, what I meant was something else:<br /> <br /> While they certainly should be far more careful with them for those reasons, &quot;ditching&quot; an Elder power isn't nearly as much of a problem in the end, that's my actual point. The game isn't nearly as affected by the specific list of Elder Powers you have as it is by the powers in the main 5 levels of a Discipline, but by all means, you should preferably have a solid list of sample elder powers (&quot;preferably&quot; since you're not a developer, just a user. The developers should have done it, period).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485345#post1485345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you here, the power's concept is great and very thematic, perhaps it could see a buff, but not a strong one.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, give it some split-second vision ability without dice bonuses attached, and a roll to determine the nature of a Time distortion. Seems strong, but are actually too circumstantial to be considered really powerful, and the best upgrade will be to ditch all the lines in higher powers that say you need to also have Auspex to do something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485345#post1485345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Clotho's Gift, I'm thinking that perhaps adding the level of Temporis as extra dices to the action to represent what the &quot;accelerated time&quot; actions could mean is a possibility. What do you think? Another possibility is to go ahead and use <i>KIss of Lachesis</i>, but give the opponent a resist roll, as I make with most &quot;I win button&quot; powers, like <i>Paws of the Newborn Curb</i>, among others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both options seem ok. As it is a level 5 power, I would give a little more &quot;oomph&quot; to the dice bonus, but just as much as the Blood cost.<br /> <br /> One option I just thought was to let the &quot;extra time&quot; specifically affect Blood use and consumption and nothing more. I don't think it is a good idea, but I do feel it may be the seed for a better one, what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T10:12:44-07:00","id":1485631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even with net successes going to damage, they're not a direct effect of Dex: you need the net successes, first. That's what I meant, while a +1 to Str will be +1 dice to damage, a +1 to Dex will do that only of it is a success on attack, which is less than 50% with dif 7 and the rule of 1.<br /> <br /> For being passive, that's countered by <b>Temporis</b> having other 4 levels of powers, so lets compare +5 Dex to 4 utility powers, including a perception one that's also passive.<br /> <br /> And the damage in <b><i>Clotho's Gift</i></b> is only for Discipline activation, if you use it under the same constrain of <b>Celerity</b> it has no damage. It isn't a better extra actions setup counterbalanced by damage, it is a better extra actions setup <i>before</i> the fact it lets you pay with damage to be even more broken. </div> </div> </div>You have some good points here, the main advantage I see in Celerity is to be ready &quot;on the fly&quot;, besides the easiness to acquire as a discipline, basically, any cainite can learn it. In fact a way to rebalance celerity has always been a problem for me, since I started ST. Revised made it a very powerful (and boring) discipline, spending 1 blood point to activate and ganing the levels in extra actions meant most combats were about extra actions and celerity was better than potence and fortitude combined. This is a &quot;place&quot; I dread coming back to. DAV20 celerity is great, but when one disallows multiple actions like I do, it loses quite a bit of effectiveness. The passive bonus is great because it adds to initiative and most combat rolls, making it a very versatile discipline, but still &quot;boring&quot;. I for once, thought about using the V5 version, but then it would create even other problems, as the fact it doesn't have advanced powers, would make it perhaps too powerful in the 1-5 levels, that's why I decided to keep it as a passive bonus, in order to reinforce its theme of being an easily accessible and &quot;practical&quot; discipline. The problem is that Temporis kind of &quot;mess with that&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why I didn't referenced DAV20, I said V20. DAV in any edition is a mixed bag as far as powers go, I never take it as default. </div> </div> </div>Still, overall I really loved the discipline's presentation on DAV20, it's one of those where they made a really good job, perhaps a bit &quot;too good&quot;, sure, but giving the game's line historic (vampire) of making lackluster discipline powers (and the fact that it's a rather rare discipline), I somehow feel tempted to turn a blind eye to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I said, give it some split-second vision ability without dice bonuses attached, and a roll to determine the nature of a Time distortion. Seems strong, but are actually too circumstantial to be considered really powerful, and the best upgrade will be to ditch all the lines in higher powers that say you need to also have Auspex to do something. </div> </div> </div>That seems like a great idea, I think I'm going to use it this way on my tables from now on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both options seem ok. As it is a level 5 power, I would give a little more &quot;oomph&quot; to the dice bonus, but just as much as the Blood cost.<br /> <br /> One option I just thought was to<b> let the &quot;extra time&quot; specifically affect Blood use and consumption and nothing more</b>. I don't think it is a good idea, but I do feel it may be the seed for a better one, what do you think? </div> </div> </div>Would you care to elaborate on that? I'm always interested in ways to enhance the systems in my games, but I think I didn't get exactly what you meant.<br /> <br /> Regarding adding Temporis to the rolls of the user for a given number of turns (for <i>Clotho's Gift</i>), I can't decide if I think it's too good or rather too weak. I think I'd need some testing, but in principle it would make what the text from <i>Clotho's Gift</i> implies, working like celerity, for &quot;extra actions&quot;, as they don't exist in my game, the bonus dice would work in the same way celerity does in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T22:01:31-07:00","id":1485680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485631#post1485631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAV20 celerity is great, but when one disallows multiple actions like I do, it loses quite a bit of effectiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've decided to stop going at it from memory and look again at Requiem's <i><b>Celerity </b></i>for ideas.<br /> <br /> There <b><i>Celerity</i></b> does not add directly to you Dex, but to your <b>Defense</b>. While WoD doesn't have such trait, I think this is a nice compromise for the worry about Dex being too powerful and makes it more flavorful at the same time: instead of acting as a flat Dex bonus, it could passively work as a defensive Dice Pool that you always have access to. You won't attack with the help of <b><i>Celerity</i></b>, but even if ten thugs attack you, with <b><i>Celerity</i></b> <b>4</b> you have a 4-dice pool against each and every attack before even declaring anything.<br /> <br /> On top of that there are the active uses: spend Blood to go first on Initiative for the round, or to interrupt someone else's action in the middle, both limited to a number of activations in a scene equal to your rank, and then the movement, where you get to multiply your movement (and movement alone) by 1+<b><i>Celerity</i></b>. I would add the option to transfer the defensive pool as a bonus to attack or to increase it as active options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485631#post1485631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you care to elaborate on that? I'm always interested in ways to enhance the systems in my games, but I think I didn't get exactly what you meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if I got it myself either! It is just a passing thought, nothing really elaborate, but for a moment I thought about the vampire using this time dilation to burn blood beyond their Generation's limit, and/or drinking it faster than the normal 3/turn limit.<br /> <br /> But as I said, is a very crude thought yet. It clearly isn't good, but I'm under the impression that something interesting can be brought from the general idea, y'know when you feel a great idea is just beyond your grasp, you know it's there but can't quite get it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T09:49:53-07:00","id":1485698,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Trying to hack the oWoD system seems like an excercise in futility, multiple actions are a pain in the ass to deal with but that is exactly what celerity is about, trying to port requiem disciplines simply doesn't work because the system is not built for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T09:59:38-07:00","id":1485700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly? Trying to hack the oWoD system seems like an excercise in futility, multiple actions are a pain in the ass to deal with but that is exactly what celerity is about, trying to port requiem disciplines simply doesn't work because the system is not built for that. </div> </div> </div>Well, I think it's quite simple to deal with. The problem is to find the best alternative for other powers that relies on multiple actions, like Temporis. In any case, I basically already found the solution, I'm going to make <i>Clotho's Gift</i> adds dice to an action to simulate the accelerated time. The thing is, multiple actions are boring and break the system, not the other way round. One great advantage of the Storyteller system is that it's easy to adapt to your stories, I think we don't &quot;lose anything&quot; not having multiple actions, quite the opposite, we gain a lot. In other words, multiple actions should be banned! Carry these words to the council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T13:17:54-07:00","id":1485712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485698#post1485698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Trying to hack the oWoD system seems like an excercise in futility, multiple actions are a pain in the ass to deal with but that is exactly what celerity is about, trying to port requiem disciplines simply doesn't work because the system is not built for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't hack the system, I just ditch it. But that said... no.<br /> <br /> A lot of people hack it because they want to keep using it for one reason or another, and hacking it isn't a huge problem. Multiple actions were the worse mechanic it ever had, and they only insisted on it because the developers at the time couldn't really avoid the &quot;simulationist&quot; approach that was too ingrained on them, so they just couldn't thought of any other way to model &quot;I'm really fast&quot; than &quot;I act more times per round&quot;. This was par of the course 90's stupidity on game design.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of it is simple, because it is just a small aspect of the game. And solving <b>Celerity</b> is simple too, because it is just one power with a simple theme to it. So much so that the hack you say to be an exercise of futility is actually something a lot of people have done, and while it was not the actual point, just a tangent, I just ported Requiem's <b>Celerity</b> just fine, how is this impossible or the system not built for that?<br /> <br /> I do agree that solving <i>every</i> problem of the WoD system is more trouble than it is worth, but that's very different from saying that ot is an exercise on futility or impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T14:13:22-07:00","id":1485716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485712#post1485712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't hack the system, I just ditch it. But that said... no.<br /> <br /> A lot of people hack it because they want to keep using it for one reason or another, and hacking it isn't a huge problem. Multiple actions were the worse mechanic it ever had, and they only insisted on it because the developers at the time couldn't really avoid the &quot;simulationist&quot; approach that was too ingrained on them, so they just couldn't thought of any other way to model &quot;I'm really fast&quot; than &quot;I act more times per round&quot;. This was par of the course 90's stupidity on game design.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of it is simple, because it is just a small aspect of the game. And solving <b>Celerity</b> is simple too, because it is just one power with a simple theme to it. So much so that the hack you say to be an exercise of futility is actually something a lot of people have done, and while it was not the actual point, just a tangent, I just ported Requiem's <b>Celerity</b> just fine, how is this impossible or the system not built for that?<br /> <br /> I do agree that solving <i>every</i> problem of the WoD system is more trouble than it is worth, but that's very different from saying that ot is an exercise on futility or impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. It's certainly not &quot;an exercise in futility&quot; trying to fix the problems of the system. I agree with everything said in this post, multiple actions were the worst mechanic in the System by a mile. It made combats EXTREMELY boring. God, how I'm relieved now that I don't use it anymore! I sometimes think about porting Requiem's Celerity to my games, it would solve many things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T08:16:27-07:00","id":1485905,"title":"","content":"DAV20\u2019s approach of allowing everyone to take multiple actions (but only one can be an attack) for -1 die and +1 difficulty to all per extra action and Celerity mostly just helping to mitigate the penalties (partially by default, totally with blood expenditure) does a lot to help keep multiple actions from getting over the top (that said we ignore the \u201cup to half your Celerity rating can be additional attacks\u201d).<br /> <br /> Applying a similar restriction to every other form of multi-action granter (i.e. still limited to 1 attack per turn) and the use of Celerity (and extra actions in general) becomes more about what extra things you can do in addition to attacking; more easily defend, move, pull off some stunt to gain an advantage, etc.; rather than just blasting your opponent with a flurry of strikes (which frankly can just be represented by the extra damage dice from a good attack roll). The automatic weapons rules for affecting multiple targets (increased difficulty, split successes between targets) works well for those times when you want to strike multiple opponents in a single turn with close combat attacks without blowing the system to little pieces too (i.e. mainly useful for taking mooks off the board).<br /> <br /> It also tends to make werewolves (and other multi-action types like certain mages) a bit more useable as potential antagonists when they can\u2019t unload with four attacks on a single target with full dice pools in a turn. Use rage to close at lightning speed, to flip the car your opponent is using for cover, and to evade their panicked attack on you while still getting a full power attack in\u2026 still lots of uses for Rage to make a werewolf a badass without taking their already ridiculous combat numbers and multiplying them across multiple attack actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T08:31:51-07:00","id":1485908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485905#post1485905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAV20\u2019s approach of allowing everyone to take multiple actions (but only one can be an attack) for -1 die and +1 difficulty to all per extra action and Celerity mostly just helping to mitigate the penalties (partially by default, totally with blood expenditure) does a lot to help keep multiple actions from getting over the top (that said we ignore the \u201cup to half your Celerity rating can be additional attacks\u201d).<br /> <br /> Applying a similar restriction to every other form of multi-action granter (i.e. still limited to 1 attack per turn) and the use of Celerity (and extra actions in general) becomes more about what extra things you can do in addition to attacking; more easily defend, move, pull off some stunt to gain an advantage, etc.; rather than just blasting your opponent with a flurry of strikes (which frankly can just be represented by the extra damage dice from a good attack roll). The automatic weapons rules for affecting multiple targets (increased difficulty, split successes between targets) works well for those times when you want to strike multiple opponents in a single turn with close combat attacks without blowing the system to little pieces too (i.e. mainly useful for taking mooks off the board).<br /> <br /> It also tends to make werewolves (and other multi-action types like certain mages) a bit more useable as potential antagonists when they can\u2019t unload with four attacks on a single target with full dice pools in a turn. Use rage to close at lightning speed, to flip the car your opponent is using for cover, and to evade their panicked attack on you while still getting a full power attack in\u2026 still lots of uses for Rage to make a werewolf a badass without taking their already ridiculous combat numbers and multiplying them across multiple attack actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before using werebeasts as antagonists, ask your players if they want to have high attrition and character turnover. If the answer is no, don't use them as antagonists. Their genre is splatter, and if they're not splattering multiple victims at once, you probably could have just used a different monster for the monster mash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T12:41:49-07:00","id":1485929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485905#post1485905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DAV20\u2019s approach of allowing everyone to take multiple actions (but only one can be an attack) for -1 die and +1 difficulty to all per extra action and Celerity mostly just helping to mitigate the penalties (partially by default, totally with blood expenditure) does a lot to help keep multiple actions from getting over the top (that said we ignore the \u201cup to half your Celerity rating can be additional attacks\u201d).<br /> <br /> Applying a similar restriction to every other form of multi-action granter (i.e. still limited to 1 attack per turn) and the use of Celerity (and extra actions in general) becomes more about what extra things you can do in addition to attacking; more easily defend, move, pull off some stunt to gain an advantage, etc.; rather than just blasting your opponent with a flurry of strikes (which frankly can just be represented by the extra damage dice from a good attack roll). The automatic weapons rules for affecting multiple targets (increased difficulty, split successes between targets) works well for those times when you want to strike multiple opponents in a single turn with close combat attacks without blowing the system to little pieces too (i.e. mainly useful for taking mooks off the board).<br /> <br /> It also tends to make werewolves (and other multi-action types like certain mages) a bit more useable as potential antagonists when they can\u2019t unload with four attacks on a single target with full dice pools in a turn. Use rage to close at lightning speed, to flip the car your opponent is using for cover, and to evade their panicked attack on you while still getting a full power attack in\u2026 still lots of uses for Rage to make a werewolf a badass without taking their already ridiculous combat numbers and multiplying them across multiple attack actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is the problem isn't ONLY how op it can be, but more so how BORING it is. Combats that take hours to conclude because of multiple actions, I've been there many times over the last 20 years, I'm very grateful that I finally decided to abolish it altogether in the last 4 years or so. There are many ways to portray Mages, Werewolves and the even more problematic in this regard Vampires extra speed (&quot;more problematic&quot; because of the general easiness of access to multiple actions and the larger pools to draw upon, etc) than using multiple actions. Multiple actions are boring to the extreme and slowdown combat scenes to a crawl. Combats are SO MUCH SMOOTHER without it, that I don't want to ever look back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T17:37:55-07:00","id":1485950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485908#post1485908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before using werebeasts as antagonists, ask your players if they want to have high attrition and character turnover. If the answer is no, don't use them as antagonists. Their genre is splatter, and if they're not splattering multiple victims at once, you probably could have just used a different monster for the monster mash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, because the rules of any setting I run are whatever I say they are, the werewolves in it can be whatever level of threat I choose for them to be. They could even have completely different origins completely divorced from the themes of WtA if I think it will make my Vampire game run more smoothly.<br /> <br /> I could say that all werewolves in my Vampire game are the cursed descendants of Lycaon who hunger for human flesh and have zero connection to Gaia because in my setting the Roman Catholic cosmology is objectively true and that, other than vampiric power and true faith (Catholic only) the only magic which exists comes in the form of Dark Thaumaturgy learned from demons because I think that those options will better fit in with the themes of my Vampire campaign. When I run a Mage game I can declare Vampires to be Thaumivores readily accepted by the collective unconscious while Werewolves are the mortal hosts of beast spirits whose cosmology is no more accurate than any other one believed in by elements of humanity because that will work better with the themes of my Mage game.<br /> <br /> Put simply; the games I run do not have to conform to your beliefs of how things should work. If you don't like that, then you're welcome to not play in games that I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T18:55:30-07:00","id":1485951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485950#post1485950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, because the rules of any setting I run are whatever I say they are, the werewolves in it can be whatever level of threat I choose for them to be. They could even have completely different origins completely divorced from the themes of WtA if I think it will make my Vampire game run more smoothly.<br /> <br /> I could say that all werewolves in my Vampire game are the cursed descendants of Lycaon who hunger for human flesh and have zero connection to Gaia because in my setting the Roman Catholic cosmology is objectively true and that, other than vampiric power and true faith (Catholic only) the only magic which exists comes in the form of Dark Thaumaturgy learned from demons because I think that those options will better fit in with the themes of my Vampire campaign. When I run a Mage game I can declare Vampires to be Thaumivores readily accepted by the collective unconscious while Werewolves are the mortal hosts of beast spirits whose cosmology is no more accurate than any other one believed in by elements of humanity because that will work better with the themes of my Mage game.<br /> <br /> Put simply; the games I run do not have to conform to your beliefs of how things should work. If you don't like that, then you're welcome to not play in games that I run.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, we can also have any interpretation of the world we see fit to our games. I remember the Gangrel used to say werewolves came from Ennoia (at least, the last time I read a Gangrel clanbook, SO MANY years ago) and if a ST likes this interpretation, all the werewolve's cosmology are nothing more than fantasy. In the end, everything in the game is subject to what the ST wants for his game. I like to use and allow werewolves and mages, esides vampires, etc, in my games, but I always tell my players that I'm a very &quot;agnostic&quot; ST, I avoid confirming what is true in the myths and what is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T19:05:42-07:00","id":1485952,"title":"","content":"This is also why the CofD's original design was constructed the way it was: the WoD's sometimes-one-world/sometimes-separate-worlds approach diminishes the utility of the game. It's one world, with half a dozen different creatures that fall under various concepts (and the potential for countless unique instances) so that you can pick what fits your game if you don't want to have to rework the PC oriented werewolves with their own corebook, and don't want to just use stat blocks with vampire powers to short-hand things. And shorted combat rounds for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T19:18:33-07:00","id":1485953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485952#post1485952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also why the CofD's original design was constructed the way it was: the WoD's sometimes-one-world/sometimes-separate-worlds approach diminishes the utility of the game. It's one world, with half a dozen different creatures that fall under various concepts (and the potential for countless unique instances) so that you can pick what fits your game if you don't want to have to rework the PC oriented werewolves with their own corebook, and don't want to just use stat blocks with vampire powers to short-hand things. And shorted combat rounds for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this lack of a &quot;one world&quot; approach makes it sometimes complicated to ST crossovers. As I said, as I have a lot of experience with crossovers and know quite a bit of every splat, I prefer to have full fleshed characters from each line in my games, but I know some ST who prefer to simplify things, like using werewolves with vampiric disciplines or the opposite, using vampires in their games with a collection of gifts and some innate powers. It's all up to the ST and the players. I only hate multiple actions and the rules of my games are somewhat closer to CofD, but I allow full fleshed characters from at least the 3 lines, i.e. Mage, Vampire and Werewolf, because I think it's &quot;cleaner&quot; this way and more fun for everyone involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T19:22:10-07:00","id":1485954,"title":"","content":"But I remember, back in the early 2000's I ST one game where Werewolves were just misguided spawns of Ennoia, but it's so long time ago I don't remember much about the game, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T19:47:05-07:00","id":1485955,"title":"","content":"With all this, I mean that WoD games varies wildly in practice. Everything is up to the ST and his group. I know one friend who has been STing Werewolf for more than 2 decades and in his games he severly limits gifts, fetishes, etc. His game is a more &quot;down to Earth&quot; version of Werewolf, where many of the things we take for granted aren't there, like some of the most powerful gifts, etc.<br /> At the same time, I had a friend who ST vampire and he once made a Tremere Councillor (I don't remember if it was Etrius, Goratrix or Meerlinda, but it doesn't matter) make a ritual that caused whooping 30 damage in a firestorm fashion. I remember back in the days I used to mock his games and call his games more &quot;Harry Potter than vampire&quot; (I was a teenager), but then again his group loved his games, and now I look back and see that who am I to judge the way other people have fun in their games? <br /> In the end, there's no such rule to determine what your game should be, etc. The most important rule is to have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T21:56:07-07:00","id":1485958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485951#post1485951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we can also have any interpretation of the world we see fit to our games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less my current approach, to.<br /> <br /> Currently I take a game line to be the actual setting of the game, then all others, while they can keep their mechanics, exist in relation to that line and subordinated to its cosmology (plus any twist I deem necessary for the story). I won't say that a player can have anything as a character only because I've accepted that sometimes we have to protect niches and themes for a given story, but that's a flexible negotiation, not a hard rule, and otherwise they can play as anything knowing that it will exist subordinated and twisted to the themes of the chronicle's main splat.<br /> <br /> I'm STing a Changeling game right now, for example, and other supernatural are actually a big part of the game, but while no particular legend will be confirmed, at the end in this chronicle they are indeed, even if they don't know, originally born within the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Other than the needs of the chronicle and the well-being of my players, nothing is sacred to me. Of course most of the time the lore, mood and themes of the games are really good, but I'll sacrifice any of them for a better game. I'll have stable Abominations, vampires that walk under the sun, stronger or weaker Paradox, anything. It doesn't mean I'll throw thing to the winds without thinking twice, but I won't stop just because it seems badwrongfun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T07:46:55-07:00","id":1485984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485929#post1485929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is the problem isn't ONLY how op it can be, but more so how BORING it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boring is subjective though. I find V20 Potence far less boring than V5 Potence because V5\u2019s is a discreet list of specific powers/widgets while V20\u2019s uses for increased strength are limited only by my imagination and whatever limits the Storyteller imposes.<br /> <br /> Celerity is similar in that increased speed and agility can be useful in a multitude of ways without adding a lot of extra complexity to keep track of.<br /> <br /> The issue with boredom as you\u2019re describing it isn\u2019t Celerity, it\u2019s the default combat structure in general that can get just as bogged down by splitting large dice pools as it can by full pool extra actions. This is mostly because the default resolution requires a minimum of four rolls where the outcome of successive ones is contingent on the prior ones (i.e. you must roll attack and defense ahead of damage and soak because the margin of the attack\u2019s success adds to the damage).<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think DAV\u2019s streamlined combat rules (i.e. skipping the damage and soak portions and limiting attack actions to once per turn) largely solve those issues and further require any uses of multiple actions to be more creative and less boring since they aren\u2019t useful for just making more attacks with. (I\u2019ll admit too that we also just count defensive actions as reflexives so combat is just an opposed roll for each person\u2019s turn).<br /> <br /> Put simply, I don\u2019t believe Celerity (or multiple non-attack actions) are the actual problem with the system and, as such, efforts spent on patching Celerity are only going to paper over a much deeper problem with the system rather than trying to solve the core problem (too many rolls required to resolve actions which in turn causes multiple actions to take disproportionately longer to resolve and turn what should feel fast paced into a grind).<br /> <br /> I think one could streamline even further than DAV20 does too if one desired. The only real consideration is how streamlined you want the end result to be. For example, some people don\u2019t mind opposed roll because it makes a fight feel more like a contest. Others want single rolls to determine the outcome because it speeds things along to areas they find more important. Neither answer is right except subjectively to one\u2019s preferences.<br /> <br /> One of the lessons I choose to take from DAV20 is that the rules are more what you\u2019d call guidelines and that individual groups shouldn\u2019t be afraid to change them to what best suits their table. The most valuable things a system can provide in this regard is a bit of inside baseball on what the math behind each of the combat stages is so it\u2019s easy to see how you can change it for your needs. Some math wonks can figure that stuff out anyway, but for the rest of us, knowing the framework helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485952#post1485952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also why the CofD's original design was constructed the way it was: the WoD's sometimes-one-world/sometimes-separate-worlds approach diminishes the utility of the game. It's one world, with half a dozen different creatures that fall under various concepts (and the potential for countless unique instances) so that you can pick what fits your game if you don't want to have to rework the PC oriented werewolves with their own corebook, and don't want to just use stat blocks with vampire powers to short-hand things. And shorted combat rounds for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disadvantage of CoD is that it\u2019s somewhat all or nothing; if the unifying cosmology of it appeals to you it allows easy crossovers. If it doesn\u2019t then you\u2019ll skip the whole thing because everything will just feel poorly fitted.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s mechanics might be better for crossovers, but it\u2019s need to be all things to all splats means it can end up being quite lukewarm in terms of feel.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the \u201ceach splat has its own themes and cosmology\u201d offers way more opportunities for a GM or player to latch onto something that appeals to them within the larger body of material and either just use it (if they\u2019re the GM) or make an appeal for its use (if they\u2019re a player).<br /> <br /> The consensual reality of Acension held appeal to me in my youth (and particularly in trying to run games with players having multiple different perspectives on truth and the way of the world), but the explicitly Biblical morality themes of earlier editions of Masquerade appeal to me strongly today. By contrast the heavy Gnosticism (which I consider a joke of a philosophy) and attendant cosmology so turned me off from Awakening that I have never had any interest in the nWoD/CoD setting.<br /> <br /> In general, I think the strong individual themes of the WoD splats are more likely to capture someone\u2019s interest than the lukewarm unifying cosmology of CoD will\u2026 the fact that we\u2019re discussing this in relation to Masquerade which was supposed to have been utterly replaced by the supposedly superior approach in CoD almost two decades ago speaks to the value of stronger and more thematic settings I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T10:50:56-07:00","id":1485993,"title":"","content":"So, in keeping with my comments above about streamlining combat, here are a couple of relevant baselines that might help in making your own adjustments.<br /> <br /> - At difficulty six, a die will succeed slightly under half the time (there's an odd inversion around four dice where you will score slightly more than half the dice rolled; 2.1 successes... but the overall range is roughly 0.45 per die to 0.42 per die within the 5-10 dice range). For ease of streamlining &quot;take half&quot; is probably close enough within most normal dice pool ranges.<br /> <br /> - A point reduction or increase in difficulty within the 4-8 range adds or subtracts about 0.1 per die from the successes scored (i.e. 5 dice at difficulty 5 will score about 0.5 more successes than 5 dice at difficulty 6). With small pools this is generally a rounding error, but at 5 dice and above (where most combat capable characters tend to fall) it will matter about half the time when you're rounding (it'll take 2.5 to 3, or 3 to 3.5... depending on how you round (up, down, closest) that might matter).<br /> <br /> - Specialization within the range of difficulty 4-8 adds about 0.1 successes scored per die (i.e. 5 dice with a specialization will score about 0.5 successes more than 5 dice without a specialization). Since specialization requires a minimum of 4 dots in something, the pools will almost always be in the range where it will add at least half a success to the outcome and so probably shouldn't just be ignored.<br /> <br /> - Extra successes on attacks only add an extra die to the damage roll each, which when rolled will only succeed half the time... so in effect, each extra success to hit adds only 0.5 successes to damage (give or take). This is important if you're wanting to streamline the damage/soak side of the equation. This also means that something which turns dice into automatic successes should only add HALF their value in extra successes as the other half has already been accounted for (Str 3 + Potence 3 used normally in V20 is 6 dice or a &quot;take half&quot; of 3. Spending blood would change the value to 4.5... 3 for full Potence successes + 1.5 for &quot;take half&quot; of the Strength 3... how you decide to round would determine if that's going to be a 4 or a 5).<br /> <br /> * * * *<br /> <br /> So, if you want to take things down to a single roll, you might use the following example; Attacker has Str 3, Dex 3, Melee 3 and is using a sword +3 damage. The defender has Dex 3, Athletics 3 and a Lethal Soak of 3. Let's say you round Soak up and Damage results down just to favor the defender slightly (you could do the opposite if you wanted a more lethal outcome).<br /> <br /> You set the damage as 3+1/2 successes. The target's Defense is 3 (subtract three successes from the attacker's result) and Soak is 2 (1.5 rounded up; subtracted from resulting damage.<br /> <br /> Attacker rolls Dex+Melee normally and scores 4 successes. That's one more than the defense so you've got a hit. You deal 1 damage 3 (base damage) + 0.5 (success by 1) - 2 (target's Soak) = 1.5 rounded down to 1.<br /> <br /> It can get a little mathematically tricky combining past that though (say a single defense target number that combines dodge and soak and a single attack value that combines the attack + damage) because of how extra hit successes add only half to resulting damage), but if you're willing to except greater or lesser lethality depending on how you do it (1/2 margin of success for less lethal that tracking defense and soak separately, full margin for more lethal than tracking them separately) then that option is available too. Keeping them separate can also be a benefit if you're regularly confronting different damage types as you need a separate soak number for each relevant one (Bashing and Lethal is often the same for vampires, but Agg is less and for humans Bashing, Lethal (from armor) and Agg (when its something armor can't stop) are going to be three different values).<br /> <br /> Mix and match to your heart's content. Personally, I like reflexive rolls for defending (particularly when players are on the receiving end and they have different values for blocking/parrying vs. dodging) and so would just use static damage (+1/2 successes) and soak to speed things up. Throw &quot;one attack per turn regardless of number of actions taken&quot; and combats run pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T10:58:45-07:00","id":1485994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485984#post1485984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disadvantage of CoD is that it\u2019s somewhat all or nothing; if the unifying cosmology of it appeals to you it allows easy crossovers. If it doesn\u2019t then you\u2019ll skip the whole thing because everything will just feel poorly fitted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely not true. It may be <u><b>your</b></u> feel with it, and it is valid as such, but that's not in any way how CoD works.<br /> <br /> Each gameline there is just as complex and thematic, and it is meant to be crossover <i>friendly</i>, not crossover <i>focused</i>. Most chronicles have no crossover at all, and my current impression is that crossovers actually happen far more in WoD than in CoD.<br /> <br /> What happens there is less of a unified cosmology and more of a policy of non-contradiction: no splat should need another to be wrong to work at all. That's hardly a &quot;be all things for all splats&quot; vs &quot;each has themes and cosmology&quot; situation. This is an ignorant comparison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485984#post1485984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast the heavy Gnosticism (which I consider a joke of a philosophy) and attendant cosmology so turned me off from Awakening that I have never had any interest in the nWoD/CoD setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you correctly describe a setting you admittedly has no interest on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484258-how-come-vampires-always-used-as-a-punching-bag-within-the-wod?p=1485984#post1485984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I think the strong individual themes of the WoD splats are more likely to capture someone\u2019s interest than the lukewarm unifying cosmology of CoD will\u2026 the fact that we\u2019re discussing this in relation to Masquerade which was supposed to have been utterly replaced by the supposedly superior approach in CoD almost two decades ago speaks to the value of stronger and more thematic settings I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think wrong. It is valid to talk about your own preference, another thing to compare two distinct games without any hard data on which is better received, ignoring the other contextual distinctions between them and in a forum dedicated to one of them, specially when there is an active forum for the other in the same site, full of fans and supporters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T11:21:23-07:00","id":1485998,"title":"","content":"I'll put up some data we can actually access:<br /> <br /> Onyx Path Kickstarters/etc. don't really indicate a significant difference between the WoD or the CofD (or Exalted, or Storypath, or D&amp;D 5e based books); including their V5 books.<br /> <br /> There's a core group that pretty much backs every project they do (yay backer credits pages!), and significant group that backs a lot of projects but is slightly more selective (their names are on all the d10 based games but not the d20 based games for example), and then more specific fans. They all sell, and they all sell pretty close to each other in terms of how many people back them (the X20 books tend to get higher pledge amounts, but for higher baseline priced giant tome core books, and those regularly get beaten by Exalted even after the Exalted 3e core book fiasco).<br /> <br /> The only difference now, is that the WoD has Paradox's large scale financial support to try to build it up as a major RPG IP again, while the other games are left to the limited reach Onyx Path has managed to establish for itself.<br /> <br /> The WoD has its strengths, the CofD has its strengths. They both appeal to new people in different ways because that's actually a good thing, not proof about one being better than the other.<br /> <br /> The reason I brought up the CofD was that it was built in direct reaction to where the WoD was in 2003... and a lot of the problems the CofD was meant to address on the mechanical side of things are also being shown to be present in the WoD5 books now that we have the H5 pdf out to pre-orderers to see what the games are going to look like over more than just V5.<br /> <br /> One of the problems is that the WoD is not &quot;each splat has its own themes and cosmology,&quot; because the WoD does crossover and thus each game doesn't actually exist in a vacuum. It exists in a Schrodinger's Box of uncertainty (which is to say, the thought experiment is silly, because we actually know the answer without opening the box: but some people are going to insist we need to open it anyway). I think people forgot how much the WoD has struggled with it's non-committal stance over the editions, and tend to assume a version of the WoD that fits their personal tastes over what the books have actually presented over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}